{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars","id":861879,"title":"Regarding the AggieCon Thread and Solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T09:08:47-07:00","id":861879,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Regarding the AggieCon Thread and Solars","content":"I was prompted to write this by the AggieCon thread. It started as a reply, but it mutated. These are just my thoughts on the matter, I'm not particularly married to them.<br /> <br /> I feel like there is an undercurrent that runs through the discussions on this forum regarding Solars. It's felt, but I rarely see it expressed. Bear with me.<br /> <br /> The Solars' core theme is &quot;Better Than You.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Solar is Sherlock Holmes, who makes everyone around him look slow and stupid.<br /> <br /> A Solar is Achilles, a single warrior who turns the tide of an entire battle, outshining everyone else on the field.<br /> <br /> A Solar is Albert Einstein, who decades after his death is being proven right experimentally, though he was operating on pure theory and math when he was alive. Entire teams of scientists and engineers work with super computers and satellites to prove what one person did with chalk and white boards(It can be more complex than that, but go with me for the sake of this example.)<br /> <br /> In RPGs, we play these people in many games not just Exalted.<br /> <br /> In real life, these people can be fucking <b>infuriating</b>.<br /> <br /> ================================================== =======<br /> <br /> How does this related to the AggieCon thread?<br /> <br /> What struck me most about the AggieCon thread was how some people made their points from the perspective of obligation, or rights. By that I mean their language itself inferred these fictional constructs we call Exalts were owed something by the developers and/or players. This is not the first time I've observed this.<br /> <br /> There were several posts in the AggieCon thread that are essentially rants at the idea of Solars &quot;taking everything,&quot; or the Dragon-Blooded &quot;having something of their own.&quot; <br /> <br /> When I unwind all that, I see two things. First, some people identify with their favorite splats so strongly that they become defensive about the splat's &quot;rights&quot;. Second, that defensiveness often comes up when the discussion turns to Solars precisely because their themes of ultimate mastery and superiority touch on that very human sensitivity. Bluntly put, when we invest emotionally in these splats, and our lovingly crafted characters are associated with them, it can be frustrating to see them &quot;outshined&quot; by Solars, in the way we have all at one point or another experienced in real life<br /> <br /> If Sherlock is a Solar, who is Watson? More importantly, who wants to play him?<br /> ================================================== ======<br /> Why does this matter?<br /> <br /> Well, I feel this way of discussing things isn't good for the game. Exalted is a make-believe world we use to play a game. As such, the only consideration that merits weight is how it plays as a game. No living being is a member of these splats. As a result, concerns of fairness are irrelevant, as long as the final product is fun for people to play. <br /> <br /> (There are two factors I'm not really addressing here. First, that not all ways of playing the game will be equally as fun, because that's impossible, and setting consistency matters because it's necessary for the kind of fun on offer in Exalted.)<br /> <br /> In fact, in Exalted, unfairness is intended. A young Solar could be a farm boy with a pitchfork and be brutally murdered by two Dragon-Blooded warriors in full Jade kit. A Dynast might be over a century-old and a master of combat, and fall to a Solar who Exalted five minutes earlier. Any of us could produce a plethora of such examples wherein each and every Exalt is the winner or the loser. <br /> <br /> Exalted is unique and fun because it sells us <b>unfairness</b>.<br /> <br /> Talking about what's &quot;fair&quot; to splats is pointless, and leads to sensitivity and/or rage. Instead, the conversation should be oriented around what's unfair in a fun way.<br /> <br /> If a given unfairness, mechanical or narrative, makes for interesting player choices, fun stories, and fits into the giant ball of unfairness that is Exalted, then it is a Good Thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:32:17-07:00","id":861901,"title":"","content":"Dude, have you <i>read</i> the Holmes books? Watson is freaking awesome. I would <i>love</i> to play him. In fact, I can think of a few times when my character has played a Watson-esque role, and I loved it.<br /> <br /> For me, my participation in that discussion wasn't motivated by wanting to give the Solars something or keep the Dragon-Blooded down. It was to point out the risks to having balanced and appealing options across the board, both for Dragon-Blooded and the Martial Arts system.<br /> <br /> I don't want to play a Dragon-Blooded graduate of the House of Bells with Archery and feel like a chump because the player across from me decided to make a Wood Dragon stylist. I don't want to play a Dodge/Thrown Dragon-Blooded character and feel shortchanged for not taking Air Dragon. I want there to be some legitimate question whether I should take Steel Devil or Fire Dragon.<br /> <br /> To me, the most elegant part of the Martial Arts system is that, if a Style fits your concept, it's a tempting (but not mandatory) option, regardless of what kind of Exalted you're playing. It should never be The Obviously Superior Choice, and I also think something is lost if it's the Obviously Inferior Choice. Without Mastery, I'm having trouble envisioning a technique where you could make it an appealing but not obviously overpowered choice for both Solars and Dragon-Blooded. The idea that some people were arguing for - that it should be BETTER for the Dragon-Blooded than for the Solars - means that it's obviously either overpowered for the Dragon-Blooded or underpowered for the Solars, and that, to my mind, is deliberately throwing away one of the best aspects of one of the better systems in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:34:18-07:00","id":861904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars#post861879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solars' core theme is &quot;Better Than You.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you hit the nail on the head for me. I don't believe that the Solars' theme is &quot;Better than You.&quot; What I love about Solars is that they are god-kings who have returned and will change the world, for good or ill. They will do this though Ability Excellence, but I don't think that means that &quot;better than the other exalts&quot;. Lunars will (I assume.) accomplish their goals though Attribute Excellence, but that doesn't mean they will be better or worse than Solars or Sidereals or the other exalts. Attribute/Ability Excellence just means a different focus, not a better focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:45:43-07:00","id":861915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars#post861879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was prompted to write this by the AggieCon thread. It started as a reply, but it mutated. These are just my thoughts on the matter, I'm not particularly married to them.<br /> <br /> I feel like there is an undercurrent that runs through the discussions on this forum regarding Solars. It's felt, but I rarely see it expressed. Bear with me.<br /> <br /> The Solars' core theme is &quot;Better Than You.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Solar is Sherlock Holmes, who makes everyone around him look slow and stupid.<br /> <br /> A Solar is Achilles, a single warrior who turns the tide of an entire battle, outshining everyone else on the field.<br /> <br /> A Solar is Albert Einstein, who decades after his death is being proven right experimentally, though he was operating on pure theory and math when he was alive. Entire teams of scientists and engineers work with super computers and satellites to prove what one person did with chalk and white boards(It can be more complex than that, but go with me for the sake of this example.)<br /> <br /> In RPGs, we play these people in many games not just Exalted.<br /> <br /> In real life, these people can be fucking <b>infuriating</b>.<br /> <br /> ================================================== =======<br /> <br /> How does this related to the AggieCon thread?<br /> <br /> What struck me most about the AggieCon thread was how some people made their points from the perspective of obligation, or rights. By that I mean their language itself inferred these fictional constructs we call Exalts were owed something by the developers and/or players. This is not the first time I've observed this.<br /> <br /> There were several posts in the AggieCon thread that are essentially rants at the idea of Solars &quot;taking everything,&quot; or the Dragon-Blooded &quot;having something of their own.&quot;<br /> <br /> When I unwind all that, I see two things. First, some people identify with their favorite splats so strongly that they become defensive about the splat's &quot;rights&quot;. Second, that defensiveness often comes up when the discussion turns to Solars precisely because their themes of ultimate mastery and superiority touch on that very human sensitivity. Bluntly put, when we invest emotionally in these splats, and our lovingly crafted characters are associated with them, it can be frustrating to see them &quot;outshined&quot; by Solars, in the way we have all at one point or another experienced in real life<br /> <br /> If Sherlock is a Solar, who is Watson? More importantly, who wants to play him?<br /> ================================================== ======<br /> Why does this matter?<br /> <br /> Well, I feel this way of discussing things isn't good for the game. Exalted is a make-believe world we use to play a game. As such, the only consideration that merits weight is how it plays as a game. No living being is a member of these splats. As a result, concerns of fairness are irrelevant, as long as the final product is fun for people to play.<br /> <br /> (There are two factors I'm not really addressing here. First, that not all ways of playing the game will be equally as fun, because that's impossible, and setting consistency matters because it's necessary for the kind of fun on offer in Exalted.)<br /> <br /> In fact, in Exalted, unfairness is intended. A young Solar could be a farm boy with a pitchfork and be brutally murdered by two Dragon-Blooded warriors in full Jade kit. A Dynast might be over a century-old and a master of combat, and fall to a Solar who Exalted five minutes earlier. Any of us could produce a plethora of such examples wherein each and every Exalt is the winner or the loser.<br /> <br /> Exalted is unique and fun because it sells us <b>unfairness</b>.<br /> <br /> Talking about what's &quot;fair&quot; to splats is pointless, and leads to sensitivity and/or rage. Instead, the conversation should be oriented around what's unfair in a fun way.<br /> <br /> If a given unfairness, mechanical or narrative, makes for interesting player choices, fun stories, and fits into the giant ball of unfairness that is Exalted, then it is a Good Thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have just answered a question that I have been thinking over since I got into the forums. I was beginning to sense something of a dislike for Solars the more I dug into the forums which I couldn't make sense of but you have explained it in a way that I didn't see before which is very enlightening.<br /> That being said I am somewhat unsure of the point of bringing this up since most of us have a predisposition towards sticking to our viewpoints...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 04-08-2016, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:45:58-07:00","id":861916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars#post861879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Solar is Sherlock Holmes, who makes everyone around him look slow and stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how unimaginative people write smart people: by having everyone else as cow-eyed dullards trawling around behind them, stupid, half-formed questions on their drool-flecked lips. &quot;The light switch, huh? The left side of the plate, what? I don't understand what is going on, you'll have to explain in elaborate detail using illustrative flashbacks.&quot; The BBC series Sherlock is a perfect example, the books are not.<br /> <br /> Things don't have to be this way. We can have characters that are not the best at everything and are also not obnoxiously incompetent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 04-08-2016, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:04:59-07:00","id":861929,"title":"","content":"How often do you think the fans who say &quot;X splat deserves to have Y and not just play lesser fiddle to Solars&quot; also mean &quot;the players who like X splat deserve to have acess to Y and not have their favorite character type always be inferior to Solars&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because okay, leaving aside for a moment the fluff that Solars are the mightiest of the Chosen (even though this by no means has to be the same as &quot;they do everything better&quot;), I think an important point is missed by outright rejecting the idea that splats don't &quot;deserve&quot; some things. Because the <i>people who like these splats and want to play characters capable of cool things</i> most certainly deserve consideration.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of fairness to imaginary things or beings per se, to me. It's a matter of <i>players having fun</i>. And (to put it in extremes that are not reflective of Exalted) I don't consider <i>fun</i> to be your favorite character type in a game being by design entirely outclassed by another in <i>every</i> possible way and their unique qualities nulled by the extended capabilities of the other type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-08-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:18:19-07:00","id":861940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861929#post861929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often do you think the fans who say &quot;X splat deserves to have Y and not just play lesser fiddle to Solars&quot; also mean &quot;the players who like X splat deserve to have acess to Y and not have their favorite character type always be inferior to Solars&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because okay, leaving aside for a moment the fluff that Solars are the mightiest of the Chosen (even though this by no means has to be the same as &quot;they do everything better&quot;), I think an important point is missed by outright rejecting the idea that splats don't &quot;deserve&quot; some things. Because the <i>people who like these splats and want to play characters capable of cool things</i> most certainly deserve consideration.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of fairness to imaginary things or beings per se, to me. It's a matter of <i>players having fun</i>. And (to put it in extremes that are not reflective of Exalted) I don't consider <i>fun</i> to be your favorite character type in a game being by design entirely outclassed by another in <i>every</i> possible way and their unique qualities nulled by the extended capabilities of the other type.</div> </div> </div> </div>This nails it. If at any point I'm playing a member of a splat and I feel &quot;man, literally everything I'm trying to do with this character would have been easier if I had just rolled a Solar&quot;, well, that's not fun. I did feel like that a couple times in 2E, playing Lunars. Once to the point of realizing that everything I had spent most of my concept on, could be done easier by simply ceding my stuff to one of the Solars in the party, and just let them do the things for me. And that feeling of &quot;I might as well have rolled a mortal here, character roleplay is the only thing I bring to this party&quot; is <i>not fun</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:24:03-07:00","id":861946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861916#post861916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things don't have to be this way. We can have characters that are not the best at everything and are also not obnoxiously incompetent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have yet to see any character, in my games or around the internet, that are best at everything. None.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:46:36-07:00","id":861960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861940#post861940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This nails it. If at any point I'm playing a member of a splat and I feel &quot;man, literally everything I'm trying to do with this character would have been easier if I had just rolled a Solar&quot;, well, that's not fun. I did feel like that a couple times in 2E, playing Lunars. Once to the point of realizing that everything I had spent most of my concept on, could be done easier by simply ceding my stuff to one of the Solars in the party, and just let them do the things for me. And that feeling of &quot;I might as well have rolled a mortal here, character roleplay is the only thing I bring to this party&quot; is <i>not fun</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the same feeling when i am playing a human in D&amp;D. &quot;man, literally everything I'm trying to do with this character would have been easier if i had just rolled a Gold dragon instead&quot;. I feel that way because a DM of mine did let me play a dragon that one time, he made them playable characters. Now every other race feels inferior.<br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder. Would we have these conversations at all, if they released the core book as a Dragonblooded splat, then released lunars, sidereal. And lastly solars. It seems to me, just because superman is a pc, other people wanna make batman into a vampire, so that he is not an irrelevant character in their eyes (he is not btw). Exalted as a game is abit different to all other games, because it has a reverse-powercreep feel in it.<br /> <br /> When i create a solar, i can buy a dragonblooded as a merit. So yeah you might feel abit useless, if you are playing a terrestrial in a celestial game <b>and your ST is downplaying the social difficulties a celestial should face.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:04:55-07:00","id":861978,"title":"","content":"Re: main post, I don't see a lot of relation to that aggiecon thread, which, to me is really about quite reasonable ideas of whether an MA in 3e can and should be able to have an essence that limits and enables certain kinds of practitioners. <br /> <br /> (Well, when it did not become about people rehashing the same arguments they made in the other thread about Dragonblooded MA, seemingly with absolutely no updating their priors based on new information that might contradicted their arguments, in ways that if I were a dev, might make me a little chary about sharing information).<br /> <br /> But in the spirit of commenting on the OP itself, I feel like that's the return of one of those memes that turned me off of the 2e-era forums a lot. No offence Totentanz, because you're from that time, and I'm having a flashback to you talking about the same meme back then, and I know seem to remember that you've always been big on the idea that one of the special things about Creation is fundamental unfairness or imbalance of power. <br /> <br /> Back to the aggiecon reaction thread, you've got a a few people in that thread (or maybe just Sanctaphrax) who were talking about &quot;Let's not talk about what these characters deserve, or what's fair to them. After all, they're just abstract characters, not people, who deserve rights and recognition and &quot;social justice&quot;.&quot;. <br /> <br /> While this is true in principle, I do feel like this does feel like, there and then, it was a bit of indirection of a underlying tendency that is very uncomfortable about talking in a positive sense about what different splats should be able to achieve, what achievable goals should be when playing them, what should be unique to each of them. If they don't deserve anything, then it's easy to sideline any discussion about what should they should positively definitely be able to do.<br /> <br /> Rather than thinking about them purely in a negative sense of how overshadowed they should be, how unfair things should be to them, what they should not be able to achieve that the Solars can, what they'll fail to do that the Solars won't fail to do, how and when they'll lose to the Solar Exalted, how their abilities are lesser than Solar ones, how they're fundamentally inept to make the places and people they love any better or safer.<br /> <br /> That's a mentality I remember fairly well. I can't remember the poster, but one 2e era conversation I can remember during a conversation was one in which a discussion about the abilities of different splats came up, and it got to the point where I was saying &quot;OK, less powerful, sure but how much less powerful? What should the odds be?&quot; and the guy I was discussing it with responded with, more or less the attitude that so long as it was less than the Solars, very much less and very obviously less, it didn't really matter. And no one seemed to find it remarkable that there was no real concern with finding a level of ability and capability that suited the splat in question, just &quot;It's balanced and well designed so long as they're very clearly lesser than Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or worse, some sort of meta reasoning from those ideas, about how the Solar Exalted represent the highest and best and most true parts of human nature, and the highest types of human person, and the only types of people who can lead humanity forward and upward, to which other ways of being and other types of people should be and naturally are subordinated. (Which is just such a narrow, narrow, hierarchical perspective on humanity and our ideals for ourselves, as people, for me).<br /> <br /> That's all an incredibly negative perspective and not one I really want to spend a lot of time in and not one that a simple one on one power difference between Solars and others automatically means we have to spend a lot of time in.<br /> <br /> The conversation around non-Solar Exalts should be fundamentally positive, about what they can do, and what is unique and true to them and how they won't simply be made irrelevant and how they can contribute and achieve their goals. Then we can season that with perhaps a little negativity about how certain things the Solars can do, they cannot. But it can't be the main dish of talking about them is just how much they can't do things and will lose against the Solars and how much they'll fail and how much they can't do anything that is both unique and desirable for humans.<br /> <br /> (That was more tl:dr than I wanted it to be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:07:53-07:00","id":861980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars#post861879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solars' core theme is &quot;Better Than You.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, although plenty of people are still carrying that baggage around from the last edition, where there were plenty of effects that worked something like &quot;upon activating this Charm, you become 1 unit of measure better than the person you're competing with. Suck it, loser!&quot; You'll notice Solars do not have any effects like that this time out.<br /> <br /> They're the reborn heroes of light, Chosen of the mightiest of the gods, brimming with the furious might of the new dawn and ready to upend Creation-- either to topple its corrupt regimes and build anew, or simply to escalate everything into a final war from which the world never recovers, it's difficult to say which. They carry with them the might of ages, returned today, <i>now</i>, demanding an immediate answer from century-spanning schemers who were not prepared for this.<br /> <br /> They're also new, confused, at odds with one another and themselves, marginalized, hunted, and trying to piece together a world of ancient secrets and forgotten power that has been largely lost or stolen.<br /> <br /> Trying to boil them down to three words always omits lots of important things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:12:28-07:00","id":861983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861980#post861980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all, although plenty of people are still carrying that baggage around from the last edition, where there were plenty of effects that worked something like &quot;upon activating this Charm, you become 1 unit of measure better than the person you're competing with. Suck it, loser!&quot; You'll notice Solars do not have any effects like that this time out.<br /> <br /> They're the reborn heroes of light, Chosen of the mightiest of the gods, brimming with the furious might of the new dawn and ready to upend Creation-- either to topple its corrupt regimes and build anew, or simply to escalate everything into a final war from which the world never recovers, it's difficult to say which. They carry with them the might of ages, returned today, <i>now</i>, demanding an immediate answer from century-spanning schemers who were not prepared for this.<br /> <br /> They're also new, confused, at odds with one another and themselves, marginalized, hunted, and trying to piece together a world of ancient secrets and forgotten power that has been largely lost or stolen.<br /> <br /> Trying to boil them down to three words always omits lots of important things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is fair, it is more positive to say why something is great than to say why everything else sucks in comparison. One of the nice things about 3ed charms are that they seem to me to focus more on what solars can do rather than how they blandly flip the table to the main rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:18:25-07:00","id":861989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars#post861879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What struck me most about the AggieCon thread was how some people made their points from the perspective of obligation, or rights. By that I mean their language itself inferred these fictional constructs we call Exalts were owed something by the developers and/or players. This is not the first time I've observed this.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Well, I feel this way of discussing things isn't good for the game. Exalted is a make-believe world we use to play a game. As such, the only consideration that merits weight is how it plays as a game. No living being is a member of these splats. As a result, concerns of fairness are irrelevant, as long as the final product is fun for people to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well said.<br /> <br /> The rest of your post is also good, but this is the bit that I wish everyone would read and agree with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861980#post861980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...there were plenty of effects that worked something like &quot;upon activating this Charm, you become 1 unit of measure better than the person you're competing with. Suck it, loser!&quot; You'll notice Solars do not have any effects like that this time out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they do. That's exactly what Living Wind Approach does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:34:39-07:00","id":862008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861901#post861901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that some people were arguing for - that it should be BETTER for the Dragon-Blooded than for the Solars - means that it's obviously either overpowered for the Dragon-Blooded or underpowered for the Solars, and that, to my mind, is deliberately throwing away one of the best aspects of one of the better systems in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is never how the game has worked. There have always been certain play styles that simply fit better for certain exalts then for others. Abyssals do necromancy better than anyone else does, if you want to play a dark brooding necromancer you got more bang for your buck as an abyssal than anyone else. The thing that makes the different types so interesting when compared to eachother is that they have strengths and weakness's. They can do things that the others simply cannot do. If every exalt was able to do every thing every other exalt could do wouldnt that make them all more dull by comparison?<br /> <br /> If everyone is equally good with the IMA then 'elemental kung fu badass' is ticked off of the list of things that make terrestirals unique in the setting compared to all the other exalt types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 04-08-2016, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:36:07-07:00","id":862009,"title":"","content":"What's usually been a sticking point about Solar Excellence, at least in my circle of friends, is that it's such a broad variety of excellence. Solars are the default splat, the corebook splat, the most played splat, and thus the one that has to be by far the most broadly capable. You couldn't launch the corebook with Sidereals or Abyssals as the default option without drastically changing new players views on the intent of setting and system. So Solars need to be just as good at being Solar Bureaucrats as Solar Martial Artists as Solar Wrestlers as Solar Survivalists. You can't get around this. Solars have been written about having no mechanical downsides (And no, the Great Curse does not count. Everyone has an equivalent), and having only in-setting downsides.<br /> <br /> On top of this broad excellence in all fields, Solars have the most immediately Big Shiny Toys. Solar Circle Sorcery. The Mastery tag. Some lines about being the best at Evocations, but we still don't have enough info to qualify what that means. Biggest motepools. Best excellency (Until you actually look at what the Sid TN fuckery Excellency does).<br /> <br /> But that's fine, as long as other splats have tools Solars can never use/take, right? Solars can't shapeshift like a Lunar can. Solars can't access the final circle of Necromancy like an Abyssal. Solars can't...do whatever the hell Infernals are doing. It's probably unwholesome. Solars can't play Cats Cradle with the strings of fate like a Sidereal. Everyone has SOME tool that Solars can't take, by nature can't even approach them in, let alone outshine them in. <br /> <br /> But to most eyes, DB don't. Dragonblooded do not have any kind of narrative protection towards &quot;This is MY tool. This is MY schtick.&quot; And to some, the social benefits of being a Dragonblooded are their actual schtick. Being able to flare without fear of a Wyld Hunt. Being able to announce your status as an Exalt and expect respect instead of (just) fear. Being able to freely own vast quantities of wealth and being able to freely display supernatural skill without fear of reprisal from the largest political entity in the world.<br /> <br /> But no mechanical schtick. Anima Flux? That's stopped by anyone with artifact armor. Tossing elemental bolts? A Brawl Solar can catch yours and toss them back harder. Or duplicate it with a hearthstone or an artifact. <br /> <br /> And I think some people look at the Immaculate Styles and are thinking, well, THAT could be the DB schtick, even though making it the DB schtick is worse for the DB splat than it is for Solars. <br /> <br /> And until we get a preview or the final copy of the DB book and we see some actual fun unique mechanics that make playing a DB as fun as it is with the dice as it is socially, people are going to search for a DB schtick, or react to them not having a schtick by trying to beef them up to the Celestial weight-class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:36:45-07:00","id":862011,"title":"","content":"As an addendum to my previous post: I agree with Totentanz. I don't think the disparate power levels of the Exalted are a problem. It really isn't about &quot;fairness&quot; between them. It's about everything still being fun, and that goal is not incompatible with the premises of the setting. It does necessitate a certain consideration to design character types who are fun, cool and desirable to play in the presence of the others, and we know the writers and developers intend for that.<br /> <br /> @Holden: Thanks for chiming in to the thread!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 04-08-2016, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:46:47-07:00","id":862024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862008#post862008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is never how the game has worked. There have always been certain play styles that simply fit better for certain exalts then for others. Abyssals do necromancy better than anyone else does, if you want to play a dark brooding necromancer you got more bang for your buck as an abyssal than anyone else. The thing that makes the different types so interesting when compared to eachother is that they have strengths and weakness's. They can do things that the others simply cannot do. If every exalt was able to do every thing every other exalt could do wouldnt that make them all more dull by comparison?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what's never how the game has worked? Dragon-Blooded being <i>individually</i> more powerful than Solars. Dragon-Blooded can be terrifying opponents, because they're probably older and more experienced, have better support and equipment, and above all, have <i>more Exalted</i> than a Solar or Lunar.<br /> <br /> In previous editions, Lunars were the best with Attributes and shapeshifting, and because of mechanical execution, maybe that didn't mean a whole lot. Hopefully this time will be better. Dragon-Blooded were the rulers of the world and had a whole society's worth of infrastructure, as well as <i>thousands</i> of themselves. A whole society of elemental super-soldiers. Again, mechanics were pretty poor, but that was the idea. Abyssals have the support of the accumulated might of Death itself, etc.<br /> <br /> <i>All Solars have</i> is that their Abilities are above and beyond anyone else's. That explicitly includes Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Martial Arts are elemental Martial Arts. Yes, they're <i>elemental,</i> but they're <i>Martial Arts.</i> By definition, Solars should be best at that, and the backer PDF doesn't shy away from that in the slightest. Dragon-Blooded will still be the best at <i>elemental</i> stuff, because they have native Charms, but as soon as you start choosing Abilities and saying <i>&quot;well, Solars don't have to be the best at THIS Ability,</i>&quot; the entire idea is flushed and we should have had Dragon-Blooded in the Core instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:47:17-07:00","id":862025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861929#post861929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often do you think the fans who say &quot;X splat deserves to have Y and not just play lesser fiddle to Solars&quot; also mean &quot;the players who like X splat deserve to have acess to Y and not have their favorite character type always be inferior to Solars&quot;?<br /> <br /> Because okay, leaving aside for a moment the fluff that Solars are the mightiest of the Chosen (even though this by no means has to be the same as &quot;they do everything better&quot;), I think an important point is missed by outright rejecting the idea that splats don't &quot;deserve&quot; some things. Because the <i>people who like these splats and want to play characters capable of cool things</i> most certainly deserve consideration.<br /> <br /> It's not a matter of fairness to imaginary things or beings per se, to me. It's a matter of <i>players having fun</i>. And (to put it in extremes that are not reflective of Exalted) I don't consider <i>fun</i> to be your favorite character type in a game being by design entirely outclassed by another in <i>every</i> possible way and their unique qualities nulled by the extended capabilities of the other type.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you said it well.<br /> <br /> When I say &quot;Dragon-Bloods deserve better&quot;, I mean the players of the Dragon-Bloods deserve better because...<br /> <br /> I don't know about everyone else, but I roleplay my fictional character. I get inside their head, try to become them, think of how <i>they</i> would react to situations, take on their voice and do some hefty escapism from reality. So when people say a splat deserves better, they're thinking of their characters, and they want them to be cool and awesome, <i>they </i>want to be cool and awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:48:07-07:00","id":862028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ncolic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861960#post861960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have the same feeling when i am playing a human in D&amp;D. &quot;man, literally everything I'm trying to do with this character would have been easier if i had just rolled a Gold dragon instead&quot;. I feel that way because a DM of mine did let me play a dragon that one time, he made them playable characters. Now every other race feels inferior.<br /> <br /> I can't help but wonder. Would we have these conversations at all, if they released the core book as a Dragonblooded splat, then released lunars, sidereal. And lastly solars. It seems to me, just because superman is a pc, other people wanna make batman into a vampire, so that he is not an irrelevant character in their eyes (he is not btw). Exalted as a game is abit different to all other games, because it has a reverse-powercreep feel in it.<br /> <br /> When i create a solar, i can buy a dragonblooded as a merit. So yeah you might feel abit useless, if you are playing a terrestrial in a celestial game <b>and your ST is downplaying the social difficulties a celestial should face.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, funny thing is, by the rules, playing a Gold Dragon in a level equivalent party would be kind of underpowered. Because Level Adjustment <i>is a thing</i> in D&amp;D. There's a reason nobody takes exotic races with strange powers, and that's because it's only rarely worth more than just having more levels. <br /> <br /> Also? Batman is a terrible example. Batman is Solar as hell, <i>as well as</i> the ST's favorite to a positively obnoxious level a large chunk of the time on top of that. But people that actually are playing the game and play with a character that has the abilities that Batman has on paper instead of the ones the writers contrive him to have (because RPGs don't have writers, they just have people playing)? Hell <b>yeah </b>they're going to feel sidelined! Batman in the Justice League requires the entire scenario to be contrived around him, or him to get a huge power up. But in a game, with five players and a GM, the player playing Batman CAN'T have the entire scenario contrived to make him come off better. Because everyone at the table gets equal share of spotlight and plot power. And in a League where J'onn J'onnz gets equal importance share to Batman, Batman is going to feel like a sidekick real quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:49:57-07:00","id":862031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862024#post862024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>All Solars have</i> is that their Abilities are above and beyond anyone else's. That explicitly includes Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well except for the Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:53:22-07:00","id":862037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862009#post862009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I think some people look at the Immaculate Styles and are thinking, well, THAT could be the DB schtick, even though making it the DB schtick is worse for the DB splat than it is for Solars.<br /> <br /> And until we get a preview or the final copy of the DB book and we see some actual fun unique mechanics that make playing a DB as fun as it is with the dice as it is socially, people are going to search for a DB schtick, or react to them not having a schtick by trying to beef them up to the Celestial weight-class.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what i want as my DB schtick, teamwork. I want exponential power ups from DB. I kinna want ;<br /> <br /> ohh look a lone DB, lets kill him and loot the artifacts ....<br /> There are 2 DB in that road ahead, we better be careful...<br /> Holy CRAP 5 DB are coming this way angryly , they could level the city!!..<br /> <br /> or<br /> a Dragonblooded is said to have the power of ten tigers.<br /> two DB has the power of 100 tigers<br /> three DB has the power of 1000 tigers<br /> 20 DB has ...holy crap they eat the whole tiger population!!<br /> <br /> making DBs schtick a knock-off of the sidereal one does not sit well for some reason.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:53:27-07:00","id":862038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862031#post862031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well except for the Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars and Abyssals get Mastery for free. Sidereals have to work at it. They are, at best, <i>differently</i> able, more able to go into the abstract stuff. Which is awesome, sure, but there's a (boring and pointless) argument to be had about which is &quot;better.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:55:35-07:00","id":862041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862024#post862024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's never how the game has worked? Dragon-Blooded being <i>individually</i> more powerful than Solars. Dragon-Blooded can be terrifying opponents, because they're probably older and more experienced, have better support and equipment, and above all, have <i>more Exalted</i> than a Solar or Lunar.<br /> <br /> In previous editions, Lunars were the best with Attributes and shapeshifting, and because of mechanical execution, maybe that didn't mean a whole lot. Hopefully this time will be better. Dragon-Blooded were the rulers of the world and had a whole society's worth of infrastructure, as well as <i>thousands</i> of themselves. A whole society of elemental super-soldiers. Again, mechanics were pretty poor, but that was the idea. Abyssals have the support of the accumulated might of Death itself, etc.<br /> <br /> <i>All Solars have</i> is that their Abilities are above and beyond anyone else's. That explicitly includes Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> The Immaculate Martial Arts are elemental Martial Arts. Yes, they're <i>elemental,</i> but they're <i>Martial Arts.</i> By definition, Solars should be best at that, and the backer PDF doesn't shy away from that in the slightest. Dragon-Blooded will still be the best at <i>elemental</i> stuff, because they have native Charms, but as soon as you start choosing Abilities and saying <i>&quot;well, Solars don't have to be the best at THIS Ability,</i>&quot; the entire idea is flushed and we should have had Dragon-Blooded in the Core instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's still the EXP gap, by a large margin considering Solar XP, so a multitude of more Charms for the Solar, plus the extra power from his own Charmset and larger mote pool. I agree with you that Dragon-Blooded are not and should not be individually more powerful than Solars, but I disagree that they cannot have Charms that are more powerful, because DBs will have less of those charms, have a harder time learning them and <b><i>they don't have supernal abilities.</i></b><br /> <br /> Seriously, even if a Dragon-Blood is better at using IMAs than Solars, Solars will be able to learn the entire style faster and cheaper than a DB ever will. And then move on to learn other MA's to increase their power, while a DB continues to struggle to the same height of power.<br /> <br /> Also, im sorry for going back in to this on this thread. Apologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:57:27-07:00","id":862045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862024#post862024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what's never how the game has worked? Dragon-Blooded being <i>individually</i> more powerful than Solars. Dragon-Blooded can be terrifying opponents, because they're probably older and more experienced, have better support and equipment, and above all, have <i>more Exalted</i> than a Solar or Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, just because they have better IMAs doesnt mean they are suddenly going to be more powerful than solars. Those five martial art styles aren't going to make up for the gap between their charm sets, sorcery, and evocations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862024#post862024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>All Solars have</i> is that their Abilities are above and beyond anyone else's. That explicitly includes Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently it doesn't explicitly include that because there are now canon martial arts that solars are no better at than anyone else. It might have worked that way in previous editions but it doesn't any longer.<br /> <br /> Back in 2e martial arts was one of the 25 abilities. Now its not. Its a merit, something that is <i>based on</i> an ability but isnt actually one itself. Charms are explicitly not things that exist in setting and martial art charms explicitly are. This seems to imply that martial arts work very differently then all the other abilities do. This in turn would seem to imply that the rule of thumb that solars are better doesn't apply because solars are only better at straightforward ability application, like you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","user":"Lionmanguy","date":". 04-08-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:01:05-07:00","id":862048,"title":"","content":"I sincerely, sincerely doubt that Solar EXP is an actual Solar-Only mechanic. Caste/Aspect-based RP bonuses would/should be system wide. It'll probably just be called Sidereal EXP when it's based on Sidereal Caste RP bonuses, Dragonblooded EXP for aspect RP bonuses, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:02:07-07:00","id":862051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862009#post862009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Anima Flux? That's stopped by anyone with artifact armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. It's stopped by Hardness but unless stated otherwise your Hardness is 0 in Initiative Crash. I could easily see a Wyld Hunt tactic of 'keep the Anathema's initiative in the negatives while our Anima Flux kills it' <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:04:12-07:00","id":862054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862051#post862051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. It's stopped by Hardness but unless stated otherwise your Hardness is 0 in Initiative Crash. I could easily see a Wyld Hunt tactic of 'keep the Anathema's initiative in the negatives while our Anima Flux kills it'</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but unless there's a bunch of native charms that interact with it in interesting ways, it still doesn't really qualify as a good mechanical schtick. I do hope DB have plenty of tools to strengthen their anima flux, learn to shape/control their anima flux, lower its intensity, etc. I remember there being charms to make Certain People immune to the DB anima flux, so you don't uh. Burn your own soldiers to death. But MORE would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11216-grindavikur","name":"Grindavikur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:05:54-07:00","id":862056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, im sorry for going back in to this on this thread. Apologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you kidding? You're actually discussing the nuts and bolts of the system without accusing me of miscellaneous favoritism-related thought-crimes. Are there half-a-dozen more of you I could talk to as well?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's still the EXP gap, by a large margin considering Solar XP, so a multitude of more Charms for the Solar,</div> </div> </div> </div>How certain are we that the Dragon-Blooded won't have their own source of bonus XP? The way it works for Solars is a great carrot for rewarding the players for good play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">plus the extra power from his own Charmset</div> </div> </div> </div>Compatibility issues for some of these, though admittedly there's some Athletics Charms and some cross-applicable stuff in Abilities like Brawl that are pretty sweet. Resistance and Dodge too, obviously, but &quot;I can survive being less skilled than you&quot; is an approach that some players would find a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and larger mote pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you that Dragon-Blooded are not and should not be individually more powerful than Solars, but I disagree that they cannot have Charms that are more powerful, because DBs will have less of those charms, have a harder time learning them</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not sure here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and <b><i>they don't have supernal abilities.</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>is</i> nice, but it stops mattering as much once the Dragon-Blooded in question gets some experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, even if a Dragon-Blood is better at using IMAs than Solars, Solars will be able to learn the entire style faster and cheaper than a DB ever will. And then move on to learn other MA's to increase their power, while a DB continues to struggle to the same height of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>You <i>might</i> have a point, but in reading the book, at no point am I getting the impression of &quot;You may not be as good as others with this Ability, but dat XP efficiency tho.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","user":"Ren9077","date":".  Tag error 04-08-2016, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:07:11-07:00","id":862059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862038#post862038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars and Abyssals get Mastery for free. Sidereals have to work at it. They are, at best, <i>differently</i> able, more able to go into the abstract stuff. Which is awesome, sure, but there's a (boring and pointless) argument to be had about which is &quot;better.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, you might be right... Let's just crack open the core and turn to page 48... Oh, well look at that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Core Page 48</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:LiberationSans\">Masters of the Martial Arts<br /> <span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Those who remember the Sidereals of old agree on one thing: they were martial artists whose <span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">genius was without compare. Only the Solar Exalted could boast equal prowess, and then only <span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">under the tutelage of a Sidereal mentor. Their mystical fighting systems, the Sidereal Martial <span style=\"color:#00000A\"><span style=\"font-family:TimesNewRomanPSMT\">Arts, are the whispered legends and ultimate secret styles of the martial arts world.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Lookie there. Solars can &quot;boast equal prowess&quot; at Martial Arts if they get tutored by a Sidereal. That doesn't sound like &quot;differently able&quot; to me, that sounds like &quot;No, Sidereals are flat-out better at Martial Arts than Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> And your comment of &quot;Sidereals have to work at [the Mastery effects]&quot; is misleading because we honestly don't know what the 'esoteric methods' to get Mastery are. It might be &quot;When a Sidereal learns the Style's Form Charm, they automatically gain the benefits of the Mastery keyword for the style&quot;. It might be that they need to buy a merit of some kind. We just don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:11:08-07:00","id":862061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862059#post862059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'know, you might be right... Let's just crack open the core and turn to page 48... Oh, well look at that!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Huh. Lookie there. Solars can &quot;boast equal prowess&quot; at Martial Arts if they get tutored by a Sidereal. That doesn't sound like &quot;differently able&quot; to me, that sounds like &quot;No, Sidereals are flat-out better at Martial Arts than Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> And your comment of &quot;Sidereals have to work at [the Mastery effects]&quot; is misleading because we honestly don't know what the 'esoteric methods' to get Mastery are. It might be &quot;When a Sidereal learns the Style's Form Charm, they automatically gain the benefits of the Mastery keyword for the style&quot;. It might be that they need to buy a merit of some kind. We just don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute.... How on earth aren't Sidereals superior Martial Artists to Solars? A Solar can reach Sidereal tier but the Tier is itself defined by Sidereals who learn what would be an epic task for a Solar just by staying alive for a few years, I am a proponent of Solars but this line of reasoning is kind of silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:13:05-07:00","id":862064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862059#post862059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>that poster named The Core Page 48, is so sure of itself, bordering arragonce!! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:14:58-07:00","id":862067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862059#post862059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Y'know, you might be right... Let's just crack open the core and turn to page 48... Oh, well look at that!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Huh. Lookie there. Solars can &quot;boast equal prowess&quot; at Martial Arts if they get tutored by a Sidereal. That doesn't sound like &quot;differently able&quot; to me, that sounds like &quot;No, Sidereals are flat-out better at Martial Arts than Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> And your comment of &quot;Sidereals have to work at [the Mastery effects]&quot; is misleading because we honestly don't know what the 'esoteric methods' to get Mastery are. It might be &quot;When a Sidereal learns the Style's Form Charm, they automatically gain the benefits of the Mastery keyword for the style&quot;. It might be that they need to buy a merit of some kind. We just don't know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I suppose there should be a caveat in my post for Sidereal Martial Arts and its reality-screwball nature.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though, I like how, in the actual Martial Arts section, the Solar and Abyssal Exalted are specifically called out as the masters of mortal Abilities, and the Sidereals can only achieve similar mastery though &quot;esoteric means.&quot; So they're better at Martial Arts, but they don't get there by just being better Martial Artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","user":"Ren9077","date":". 04-08-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:23:18-07:00","id":862075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grindavikur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862054#post862054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but unless there's a bunch of native charms that interact with it in interesting ways, it still doesn't really qualify as a good mechanical schtick. I do hope DB have plenty of tools to strengthen their anima flux, learn to shape/control their anima flux, lower its intensity, etc. I remember there being charms to make Certain People immune to the DB anima flux, so you don't uh. Burn your own soldiers to death. But MORE would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think they should more or less take weaponised Environmental Hazards for themselves. Of the existing Exalted there's only really Green Sun Princes that I feel have any real thematic claim to them, if any Exalt should go &quot;you're too close to me, now you count as standing in a bonfire!&quot; it's Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:24:00-07:00","id":862076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862056#post862056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you kidding? You're actually discussing the nuts and bolts of the system without accusing me of miscellaneous favoritism-related thought-crimes. Are there half-a-dozen more of you I could talk to as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! Only me! *muffled yelling from the basement* &lt;__&lt;; there's....there's only one me here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How certain are we that the Dragon-Blooded won't have their own source of bonus XP? The way it works for Solars is a great carrot for rewarding the players for good play. </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're actually completely correct, here. If i'm not mistaken, Solar XP is a <i>type</i> of experience, and not only applicable to Solars. I'm almost certain i read that somewhere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> That <i>is</i> nice, but it stops mattering as much once the Dragon-Blooded in question gets some experience. </div> </div> </div>Well, probably, but that's likely a <i>lot</i> of experience. I mean, the rarity of actually getting to Essence 4 or 5, wherever the capstone of these Charms ends, takes a while to get to. Unfortunately, for me at least, my games don't generally last to that point, so actually playing a Dragon-Blooded master of a style doesn't seem probable. A Solar would be able to as soon as he got the exp for the Charms or just take them out of the gate, if he went Supernal with it.<br /> <br /> He really can master in weeks what could take a DB months or years to learn, and that's for PCs! Which is kind of cool. If a Solar had convinced an Immaculate to actually reveal the secrets of his fighting style and was teaching him and &quot;This technique will take you at least three mo-.....how-...thats...not even fair.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You <i>might</i> have a point, but in reading the book, at no point am I getting the impression of &quot;You may not be as good as others with this Ability, but dat XP efficiency tho.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's true. Also, in regards to the exp disparity, since we don't have the DB book, we don't know how that'll influence stuff. But this quoted point is actually a really good one.<br /> <br /> Skill-wise, a Solar will likely be every bit as good at using the techniques as a Dragon-Blood, even better, since he will *probably be able to learn them faster and cheaper. But I believe the Arts will have interaction with a DB's Anima that are unique to them only, and that will be what gives them the edge over the opposition, things like I stated in the other thread, such as a constant water source, grappling with a destructive anima, lifting everyone (user included) a mile into the air to drop....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:29:50-07:00","id":862080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862076#post862076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, probably, but that's likely a <i>lot</i> of experience. I mean, the rarity of actually getting to Essence 4 or 5, wherever the capstone of these Charms ends, takes a while to get to. Unfortunately, for me at least, my games don't generally last to that point, so actually playing a Dragon-Blooded master of a style doesn't seem probable. A Solar would be able to as soon as he got the exp for the Charms or just take them out of the gate, if he went Supernal with it.<br /> <br /> He really can master in weeks what could take a DB months or years to learn, and that's for PCs! Which is kind of cool. If a Solar had convinced an Immaculate to actually reveal the secrets of his fighting style and was teaching him and &quot;This technique will take you at least three mo-.....how-...thats...not even fair.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but a Dragon-Blooded at Essence 3 or so is probably going to be scary, with or without special exclusive IMA tricks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862041#post862041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true. Also, in regards to the exp disparity, since we don't have the DB book, we don't know how that'll influence stuff. But this quoted point is actually a really good one.<br /> <br /> Skill-wise, a Solar will likely be every bit as good at using the techniques as a Dragon-Blood, even better, since he will *probably be able to learn them faster and cheaper. But I believe the Arts will have interaction with a DB's Anima that are unique to them only, and that will be what gives them the edge over the opposition, things like I stated in the other thread, such as a constant water source, grappling with a destructive anima, lifting everyone (user included) a mile into the air to drop....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not against Dragon-Blooded having access to these tricks. What I <i>am</i> against is having them tied to Immaculate Martial Arts. In addition to the issues we've discussed so far, it leads to another big issue: Why can't a Melee Dragon-Blooded use the elements like this? That's kind of what the whole premise of &quot;elemental super-soldier&quot; is about!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:46:10-07:00","id":862095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862080#post862080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not against Dragon-Blooded having access to these tricks. What I <i>am</i> against is having them tied to Immaculate Martial Arts. In addition to the issues we've discussed so far, it leads to another big issue: Why can't a Melee Dragon-Blooded use the elements like this? That's kind of what the whole premise of &quot;elemental super-soldier&quot; is about!</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the devs have said they plan on incorporating elemental themes all over the regular charm sets. So like even though melee is fire, there might be wind stirke melee stuff. So thats a plus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:53:12-07:00","id":862103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862080#post862080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not against Dragon-Blooded having access to these tricks. What I <i>am</i> against is having them tied to Immaculate Martial Arts. In addition to the issues we've discussed so far, it leads to another big issue: Why can't a Melee Dragon-Blooded use the elements like this? That's kind of what the whole premise of &quot;elemental super-soldier&quot; is about!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I would imagine that the Melee charms of the DB's do interact with their Anima's in such a fashion. Wasn't there some dev statement saying that at least certain elementally themed db Charms would actually be five charms in one, one for each element? Or something. I could be wrong or it could've changed,my memory is fuzzy.<br /> <br /> But what I am saying is that, without Mastery, Dragon-Bloods and Solars (and anyone else) are learning the exact same Charms. Say there was an Air Dragon Charm that, after successfully striking your opponent with a withering attack, it launched everyone within close range four range bands into the air. An Air Aspect would be fine, as they can fall from any distance safely. A Solar may or may not be, depending on any other Charms he may have, a Lunar would be fine if they can sprout wings, etc... Just the Style itself could have more potent effect since it wouldn't have to safely protect the user from side effects or even contain the power of the techniques to opponents, since they're largely immune to their own elemental aspects.<br /> <br /> Its a powerful, but much more dangerous style, for other Exalts to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:53:26-07:00","id":862104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862095#post862095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the devs have said they plan on incorporating elemental themes all over the regular charm sets. So like even though melee is fire, there might be wind stirke melee stuff. So thats a plus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know. These exclusive benefits that people are asking to get with Immaculate Martial Arts would be <i>far</i> better structured, in my opinion, as native Charms not strictly related to Martial Arts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:55:17-07:00","id":862107,"title":"","content":"As a Solar player, I feel the world is a better place because [that one Lunar player with the My Little Pony avatar] has written long and detailed rants about how Solars suck and how Lunars deserve so much better than they get.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue for me isn't that people are enthusiastic and devoted to a certain splat, but that communication quickly falls into this place where we're not listening to one another and repeating the same things in a different way. I prefer productive discussions. Reading from page 1 to page 6 ought to give me a sense of forward movement.<br /> <br /> I do see Solars as being &quot;the best at what they do.&quot; They're paragons of human ability. A dedicated Solar swordsman will be a better sword fighter than a Lunar. This has nothing to do with whether any specific Lunar charm that can be used while swordfighting is superior to a Solar Melee charm or not. Nor does it mean that the Solar will always beat the Lunar in a swordfight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:55:57-07:00","id":862110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862103#post862103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I would imagine that the Melee charms of the DB's do interact with their Anima's in such a fashion. Wasn't there some dev statement saying that at least certain elementally themed db Charms would actually be five charms in one, one for each element? Or something. I could be wrong or it could've changed,my memory is fuzzy.<br /> <br /> But what I am saying is that, without Mastery, Dragon-Bloods and Solars (and anyone else) are learning the exact same Charms. Say there was an Air Dragon Charm that, after successfully striking your opponent with a withering attack, it launched everyone within close range four range bands into the air. An Air Aspect would be fine, as they can fall from any distance safely. A Solar may or may not be, depending on any other Charms he may have, a Lunar would be fine if they can sprout wings, etc... Just the Style itself could have more potent effect since it wouldn't have to safely protect the user from side effects or even contain the power of the techniques to opponents, since they're largely immune to their own elemental aspects.<br /> <br /> Its a powerful, but much more dangerous style, for other Exalts to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sold on this approach. It works for your example, but I don't see it working in a broader sense. What's the Fire Dragon equivalent? Burning someone <i>and</i> yourself, because you're not immune to flame conjured by your own technique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:08:25-07:00","id":862123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861901#post861901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that some people were arguing for - that it should be BETTER for the Dragon-Blooded than for the Solars - means that it's obviously either overpowered for the Dragon-Blooded or underpowered for the Solars, and that, to my mind, is deliberately throwing away one of the best aspects of one of the better systems in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I was one of those people, though my post was mostly a rage-induced hyperbole reaction to what was going on in that thread (That's why I bowed out at that point. ). I don't really want Dragonblooded to be better at IMA than Solars, I just don't see why Solars should get special powers for IMA when that MA wasn't designed for them both in and out of the setting. We can agree to disagree on that point though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:11:25-07:00","id":862125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862123#post862123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit I was one of those people, though my post was mostly a rage-induced hyperbole reaction to what was going on in that thread (That's why I bowed out at that point. ). I don't really want Dragonblooded to be better at IMA than Solars, I just don't see why Solars should get special powers for IMA when that MA wasn't designed for them both in and out of the setting. We can agree to disagree on that point though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lack of a Mastery keyword at least doesn't mean DBs will be better at IMA than Solars. Just that Solars won't be better at using the IMA charms than DBs. I'm onboard with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:12:52-07:00","id":862129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862125#post862125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lack of a Mastery keyword at least doesn't mean DBs will be better at IMA than Solars. Just that Solars won't be better at using the IMA charms than DBs. I'm onboard with that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know that, but my rage filled self from yesterday forgot that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:19:42-07:00","id":862135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862123#post862123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit I was one of those people, though my post was mostly a rage-induced hyperbole reaction to what was going on in that thread (That's why I bowed out at that point. ). I don't really want Dragonblooded to be better at IMA than Solars, I just don't see why Solars should get special powers for IMA when that MA wasn't designed for them both in and out of the setting. We can agree to disagree on that point though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a point about Wing Chun kung fu in the other thread. That style was, according to legend, designed by a woman, for a woman. Its most famous practitioner? Bruce Lee. It wasn't designed for him, but that didn't stop him from mastering every bit of that style. (Plus some others, and then created his own, yeah, but that's outside the scope of the metaphor.)<br /> <br /> Let's look at the Martial Arts system as it stands. We know that Solars and Abyssals are, for this purpose, basically identical. So what happens when Laughing Wounds Style comes out? That's designed for Abyssals, not Solars. Should Abyssals get a special bonus that no one else gets? If Throne Shadow is a well-designed style, this makes the Abyssal an inherently superior Martial Artist than a Solar can ever be. Why should we allow this?<br /> <br /> What happens when a Solar looks at the Immaculate Martial Arts and Throne Shadow and develops a Solar Martial Arts Style called &quot;F*** You I'm the Best&quot; and it inherently has a bonus that's only for Solars. Is that okay?<br /> <br /> Both of these things are perfectly fine by the logic you're using to boost Immaculate Martial Arts for the Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","user":"Ren9077","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:19:49-07:00","id":862136,"title":"","content":"I don't think IMA being better for DBs is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> I want to add here that we have one book out of the entire line. We don't know how the IMAs were developed. What if instead of the Sidereals making the Terrestrial's best martial arts, this was actually something the early dragon-blooded developed by studying with the Elemental Dragons themselves?<br /> <br /> Yes, there's a brief summary on a splash page telling us that Solars are the best Martial Artists, but that doesn't mean that Solars can master every MA or do so with as much skills as other beings.<br /> <br /> It's just, I don't understand how we can take a couple of paragraphs from the core and extrapolate a set of comprehensive and immutable truths about the setting. Especially as one of the things I'm looking forward to in Exalted 3rd is a sense of newness. That I'm not simply retreading facts established in previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862135#post862135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a Solar looks at the Immaculate Martial Arts and Throne Shadow and develops a Solar Martial Arts Style called &quot;F*** You I'm the Best&quot; and it inherently has a bonus that's only for Solars. Is that okay?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that bonus called Mastery?<br /> <br /> Because that's the name of the Solaroid-only bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:24:27-07:00","id":862141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862135#post862135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens when Throne Shadow comes out? That's designed for Abyssals, not Solars. Should Abyssals get a special bonus that no one else gets? If Throne Shadow is a well-designed style, this makes the Abyssal an inherently superior Martial Artist than a Solar can ever be. Why should we allow this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for starters, Throne Shadow was the name given to the Errata'd Sidereal Hero Style in 2E.<br /> <br /> Are you thinking of Hungry Ghost or Laughing Wounds Style?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:30:07-07:00","id":862150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862141#post862141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well for starters, Throne Shadow was the name given to the Errata'd Sidereal Hero Style in 2E.<br /> <br /> Are you thinking of Hungry Ghost or Laughing Wounds Style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I'm freaking tired, since last weekend's ALL-FREAKING-NIGHT Magic tournament. I mean the thing you said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:32:24-07:00","id":862152,"title":"","content":"I, for one, am comfortable with Laughing Wounds Style working better with the guys that can Exalt after being beheaded.<br /> <br /> Edit: And the guys that can, maybe, be beheaded <i>after</i> -- Liminals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:36:31-07:00","id":862154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862110#post862110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sold on this approach. It works for your example, but I don't see it working in a broader sense. What's the Fire Dragon equivalent? Burning someone <i>and</i> yourself, because you're not immune to flame conjured by your own technique?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! In a way. Perhaps your Burning Seething Raging Claw of the Fire Dragon is a multiple action charm, allowing you to strike every opponent with a withering attack at close range, and for every successful strike, you get a single die of damage to be added to an environmental hazard to be used on everything at short range, as a wave of fire explodes around you, lighting every flammable thing on fire. Well, a Fire Aspect is immune to flame while his banner is up, so he escapes that effect, but others may not be so lucky.<br /> <br /> Of course, a Solar, for example, could be wearing an artifact thong that protects him from fire, or have certain resistance Charms that get him through the effect.<br /> <br /> If the Wood Dragon still gets Bows as form weapons, you could create a magical arrow that is completely coated in poison barbs, so you cannot touch it bare handed without getting scraped, making removal of it very dangerous. For a wood aspect, immune to poison, this is fine, perhaps a bashing or lethal damage is taken, but for anyone else, they have to wear thick gloves or gauntlets or suffer the poison. If you don't have a bow, its your own hand that becomes poisonously barbed, and if you're not a wood dragon, you must suffer the poison.<br /> <br /> Who knows what neat effects you can create when you don't need to worry about your own safety?<br /> <br /> *edit: Also, a kind of neat thought. Maybe there's a very, very good reason they don't <i>use</i> Mastery Effects. The styles may indeed have them except...using those talents to such a degree would literally kill the user, as elemental essence backfires and destroys them. DB's can't access those effects, and it'd kill anyone else, so having them in there would be unreasonable.<br /> <br /> :.P maybe? Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","user":"Arteliex","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:38:28-07:00","id":862156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862154#post862154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Wood Dragon still gets Bows as form weapons,</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight point... In the big leak, there were actually Water and Wood Stylists in the Sample Antagonist section. The Wood Dragon Monk used a staff rather than a bow. Just throwing that out there.<br /> <br /> Then again, they might change it by the time the DB book comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:42:37-07:00","id":862160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862154#post862154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! In a way. Perhaps your Burning Seething Raging Claw of the Fire Dragon is a multiple action charm, allowing you to strike every opponent with a withering attack at close range, and for every successful strike, you get a single die of damage to be added to an environmental hazard to be used on everything at short range, as a wave of fire explodes around you, lighting every flammable thing on fire. Well, a Fire Aspect is immune to flame while his banner is up, so he escapes that effect, but others may not be so lucky.<br /> <br /> Of course, a Solar, for example, could be wearing an artifact thong that protects him from fire, or have certain resistance Charms that get him through the effect.<br /> <br /> If the Wood Dragon still gets Bows as form weapons, you could create a magical arrow that is completely coated in poison barbs, so you cannot touch it bare handed without getting scraped, making removal of it very dangerous. For a wood aspect, immune to poison, this is fine, perhaps a bashing or lethal damage is taken, but for anyone else, they have to wear thick gloves or gauntlets or suffer the poison. If you don't have a bow, its your own hand that becomes poisonously barbed, and if you're not a wood dragon, you must suffer the poison.<br /> <br /> Who knows what neat effects you can create when you don't need to worry about your own safety?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a novel approach, but I don't see it as adding to the fun in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:42:42-07:00","id":862161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862154#post862154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, a Solar, for example, could be wearing an artifact thong that protects him from fire</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my new headcanon for Wolfer's fight in the tea-shop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T15:47:10-07:00","id":862229,"title":"","content":"Seeing how this instantly turned into a carbon-copy of the other thread, and was framed in a way that made that a pretty likely outcome, it seems to have been a bad idea to make a new thread for it. The impression left is that the post belonged in the other thread, but was put here so more people should notice it.<br /> <br /> This really grinds my gears! I should make a thread about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:22:40-07:00","id":862433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862229#post862229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing how this instantly turned into a carbon-copy of the other thread, and was framed in a way that made that a pretty likely outcome, it seems to have been a bad idea to make a new thread for it. The impression left is that the post belonged in the other thread, but was put here so more people should notice it.<br /> <br /> This really grinds my gears! I should make a thread about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No! Stop, lest you make the same mistake I did during the craft conflicts! We don't need Immaculate Incursions on the board!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:29:01-07:00","id":862440,"title":"","content":"Personally, if I were running a forum, and somebody started a new thread to offer meta-commentary on another thread instead of addressing it directly, that would result in a thread-merge and a polite request to Not Do That Again. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T22:51:20-07:00","id":862449,"title":"","content":"Okay then let's bring the thread back on track and away from IMA!!!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=861940#post861940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This nails it. If at any point I'm playing a member of a splat and I feel &quot;man, literally everything I'm trying to do with this character would have been easier if I had just rolled a Solar&quot;, well, that's not fun. I did feel like that a couple times in 2E, playing Lunars. Once to the point of realizing that everything I had spent most of my concept on, could be done easier by simply ceding my stuff to one of the Solars in the party, and just let them do the things for me. And that feeling of &quot;I might as well have rolled a mortal here, character roleplay is the only thing I bring to this party&quot; is <i>not fun</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So....why don't you just play a Solar then? Solars are versatile as fuuuuuuck. They can be basically anything you want them to be, that's one of their jobs, being the core book splat. What do you like about the other splats that you can't just add to your Solar character, and then have somebody who's fun for you to play, and simultaneously the unquestioned power in their chosen field?<br /> <br /> This comment isn't directed at you specifically, Drascin, but everyone in the thread who shares your sentiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:17:22-07:00","id":862466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862125#post862125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lack of a Mastery keyword at least doesn't mean DBs will be better at IMA than Solars. Just that Solars won't be better at using the IMA charms than DBs. I'm onboard with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, actually, it doesn't even mean that. It literally means, and only means, that Solars won't be <i>able to use the Mastery keyword to be</i> better at using the IMA charms than DBs. We <i>don't know</i> how any other aspect of the design of the IMAs works. Everything beyond that is speculation -- perhaps reasonable speculation, but still just speculation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T23:27:06-07:00","id":862472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862449#post862449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So....why don't you just play a Solar then? Solars are versatile as fuuuuuuck. They can be basically anything you want them to be, that's one of their jobs, being the core book splat. What do you like about the other splats that you can't just add to your Solar character, and then have somebody who's fun for you to play, and simultaneously the unquestioned power in their chosen field?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think their point is that a PC shouldn't be made utterly superfluous by the presence of Solars. You're right, Solars do things well. <i>You shouldn't need to play a Solar if you want to contribute</i>. If you're sitting there, feeling like your character is deadweight just because you're a Dragonblood, and there's a Solar in the group... That's not fun. A person playing a DB for character reasons shouldn't have every attempt to do something be met with &quot;Nah, we'll just let That Solar do it, they're better&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862466#post862466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, actually, it doesn't even mean that. It literally means, and only means, that Solars won't be <i>able to use the Mastery keyword to be</i> better at using the IMA charms than DBs. We <i>don't know</i> how any other aspect of the design of the IMAs works. Everything beyond that is speculation -- perhaps reasonable speculation, but still just speculation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Point. I've been out-pedantic'd, bravo good sir. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T01:11:54-07:00","id":862508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862472#post862472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You shouldn't need to play a Solar if you want to contribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is meaningless. There is no standard for &quot;contribute.&quot; I can shout loudly and &quot;contribute.&quot; <br /> <br /> Also, as I've said before elsewhere, no Dawn Caste can, by himself, make the presence of another character superfluous, because one person is not, cannot be two people.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Even the Solar Supernal Socialize PC has to switch from one persona to another, he doesn't get to just play both simultaneously!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T02:18:09-07:00","id":862526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862508#post862508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is meaningless. There is no standard for &quot;contribute.&quot; I can shout loudly and &quot;contribute.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, as I've said before elsewhere, no Dawn Caste can, by himself, make the presence of another character superfluous, because one person is not, cannot be two people.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Even the Solar Supernal Socialize PC has to switch from one persona to another, he doesn't get to just play both simultaneously!</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming Ant and Starfish Trick doesn't make it into 3e.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like it if, save for some partiulars (sorcery, martial arts, crafting n/a artifacts), DB charms were as a whole fairly competitive with solar charms (and lunar, sidereal, liminal, gentimian, abyssal, infernal, alchemical, blankity-blankal, WHATEVER), maybe costing more experience or requiring more experience to get higher essence. Dragonblooded as a whole would still be weaker than solars because of dice caps and excellencies and supernals and sorcery/martial arts/crafting, and the setting's &quot;Solars are the mightiest of the Exalted&quot; doesn't <i>necessarily </i>have to be reflected in the individual case of PCs who are already exceptional among the exceptional by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T02:21:41-07:00","id":862528,"title":"","content":"I'd rather DB charms generally were weaker, because that's (part of) the point of DBs. To a DB, a Solar is very scary, hence the whole Wyld Hunt. And when you want a less high-powered game of Exalted, you can play Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> Not to say that it's essential that everything is weaker, but overall, certainly.<br /> <br /> Which again, doesn't mean they can't contribute, as Alucard says. Unless you are trying to do the exact same thing as a Solar (except combat, because in combat everyone gets a go so no-one is utterly superfluous).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T04:49:43-07:00","id":862548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862135#post862135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens when Laughing Wounds Style comes out? That's designed for Abyssals, not Solars. Should Abyssals get a special bonus that no one else gets?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Abyssals had native charms that were similar to what Laughing Wounds already offered then I'd appreciate the style acknowledging that and offering them extra incentives to learn it because if it doesn't do that it risks becoming the style for people pretending to be an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Edit: For the sake of clarity, I'm assuming it would reappear in the Abyssals book. If it featured in a MA compendium like last time then I probably wouldn't give Abyssals any special incentives beyond Mastery since the strength of their connection to the style would be its creation by a Deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-09-2016, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T06:04:20-07:00","id":862567,"title":"","content":"I think the question of how different Exalted work out in play needs to acknowledge certain points about how player groups should organise. I mean, if you're playing a Dragon Blood and feel that you're being overshadowed by another player who is a Solar... why does one group have two people who are trying to do such similar things in a manner other than playing out cooperation? Is that something that would be better if they were both Solars? Wouldn't that just change it from &quot;I'm being overshadowed&quot; to &quot;I have to fight for limited access to every gameplay opportunity for our group's niche&quot;?<br /> <br /> If it's a question of &quot;I'm playing this Dragon Blood, but can't help feel that this concept would be done better if it was the exact same thing as some theoretical Solar who isn't actually present in the game&quot;, well, some of that does depend on giving other Exalted distinct gameplay mechanisms that create unique and fun forms of play, but some of it requires one to buy into the setting details provided around the different Exalted types (of which Dragon Blooded have one of the most distinct), and some of it is just something that somebody is going to have to get over. It's like, if you're looking for an optimized play experience or group role, then no, you're not getting that while playing other Exalted; the game is never going to act as though it's waiting beyond the core for all of the basic tools for a complete play experience.<br /> <br /> It all comes back from the really early design conceit of a pulp fantasy game set in a world close to the end in which ancient heroes whose absence is the major factor in why things went down inexplicably return, and Grabowski's realization of &quot;hey, if we set this thing up as important and then wait to reveal it, it will never really live up to the build up, so it would be more functional to start by defining the top and then working out from there&quot;. I, personally, will always appreciate that, since I've had too many experiences with things in which something was continuously built up to be the greatest ultimate thing and then floundered in the execution.<br /> <br /> Heh, of all the things to first think of for this, it reminds me of how in Frasier they initially didn't want to make another version of the unseen wife character from Cheers, but eventually had so much fun coming up with outlandish descriptions of Maris Crane that they realised that no human actor could actually portray her, so they just stuck with jokes for the outlandish descriptions. That's a case in which you turn the limitations of the reveal into a strength, but obviously you can't really do that so effectively for significant actors in a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> Works better for the Yozis, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T09:08:58-07:00","id":862605,"title":"","content":"This is one of those topics that can really only be addressed in the context of the previous two versions. Since the only thing out for 3rd edition at this time is the PDF file for backers and even that is having changes made to it before final release of the core rule book.<br /> <br /> Historically speaking this is how the Exalted have always broken down.<br /> Solars are champions, heroes and personify perfection in all things. But they are not the masters of everything.<br /> Lunars have always been bdf's. You really don't play a Lunar if you are looking for an intellectual. They start as better fighters than Solars, but get bogged down by higher experience costs.<br /> Sidereals are just jackholes. They mess with people. Sure they have the best and most broken martial arts, but primarily they change the odds. Things get easier for them and harder for their opponents. A Sidereal doesn't need to hit you to make you wish that you hadn't gotten out of bed in the morning. Worst day ever.<br /> Dragon Blooded are suppose to be about numbers and cooperation. Personally, I've always thought that the Sidereals have had the better caste abilities for working as a team. What Dragon Blooded really have is very essence efficient charms. I.E. in 2nd ed. their 1st excellency gave 2 dice per mote of essence spent. Which kind of makes up for the smaller essence pool. This same thing happened with Paladins in WoW. They became the best healers because they had smaller mana pools that they could regenerate faster and their healing charm costs were reduced to reflect the smaller pools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T10:47:47-07:00","id":862654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862472#post862472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think their point is that a PC shouldn't be made utterly superfluous by the presence of Solars. You're right, Solars do things well. <i>You shouldn't need to play a Solar if you want to contribute</i>. If you're sitting there, feeling like your character is deadweight just because you're a Dragonblood, and there's a Solar in the group... That's not fun. A person playing a DB for character reasons shouldn't have every attempt to do something be met with &quot;Nah, we'll just let That Solar do it, they're better&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but what I'm saying is, those character reasons might fit a Solar too, in which case you can just be a Solar and have all the power and all the freedom. Are you playing a DB because you like the whole elemental warrior thing? Grab evocations, martial arts and enjoy all your powerful solar charms while still hurling thunderbolts. <br /> <br /> Are you playing a Sidereal because you like the idea of a shadowy, unseen manipulator who's never properly remembered? Solar social and stealth charms definitely let you do that. They let you do it in a more straightforward and powerful way even. Which doesn't even mean they lack finesse or anything, you can still be super clever and graceful while using them.<br /> <br /> Other than splat loyalty or prejudice, which are kind of silly, why not just play a Solar whenever you want to make sure that you won't be overshadowed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862528#post862528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which again, doesn't mean they can't contribute, as Alucard says. Unless you are trying to do the exact same thing as a Solar (except combat, because in combat everyone gets a go so no-one is utterly superfluous).</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, yes and no. If you're playing a supposedly badass fire aspected swordsman or something who's fighting alongside a solar circle for some reason, fighting a second circle demon like Octavian could lead to situations where the dawn deals 24 initiative damage to him, knocking him down from 30, then you throw everything you've got at him and deal another 3 damage.<br /> <br /> In that scenario, true, you technically helped, but when you made your character to be a theoretically powerful fighter, it can suck to be so far behind another player, you're not really doing the job you wanted to do. Especially when the Twilight who picked up a brawl charm or two goes ahead and crashes the guy with another 10 damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's even playing to your strengths, DBs with combat, Sidereals to espionage, Lunars with infiltration and adaptability. Let's instead look at more obvious examples, the DB socialite or lore master. DBs have like, 2-3 very situational presence charms that actually aid in social combat, and maybe one really shifty one for lore that helps with speed reading books. It's much easier in those contexts to see why a DB player might feel like the Solar who grabbed 3 social charms is making him auperfluous. Also a really good reason why that player should have rolled up the rim to win. The rim in this context being a Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T12:48:31-07:00","id":862707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862654#post862654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but what I'm saying is, those character reasons might fit a Solar too, in which case you can just be a Solar and have all the power and all the freedom. Are you playing a DB because you like the whole elemental warrior thing? Grab evocations, martial arts and enjoy all your powerful solar charms while still hurling thunderbolts.<br /> <br /> Are you playing a Sidereal because you like the idea of a shadowy, unseen manipulator who's never properly remembered? Solar social and stealth charms definitely let you do that. They let you do it in a more straightforward and powerful way even. Which doesn't even mean they lack finesse or anything, you can still be super clever and graceful while using them.<br /> <br /> Other than splat loyalty or prejudice, which are kind of silly, why not just play a Solar whenever you want to make sure that you won't be overshadowed.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense Monkey, but that train of thought right there is probably a significant reason for people who hate Solars. I don't <i>want</i> to have to play a Solar with Evocations if I want to play a Dragon Blood. I shouldn't <i>have</i> to play a Solar with Social and Stealth to be a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <i>Solars shouldn't be better Dragon Bloods and Sidreals than Dragon Bloods and Sidereals</i>. That's the whole point.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I'm saying this as a guy who loves Solars. Like, Solars are my second-favorite splat! (Sids being the first, and Dragon Bloods being third)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-09-2016, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:11:16-07:00","id":862721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862548#post862548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Abyssals had native charms that were similar to what Laughing Wounds already offered then I'd appreciate the style acknowledging that and offering them extra incentives to learn it because if it doesn't do that it risks becoming the style for people pretending to be an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> Edit: For the sake of clarity, I'm assuming it would reappear in the Abyssals book. If it featured in a MA compendium like last time then I probably wouldn't give Abyssals any special incentives beyond Mastery since the strength of their connection to the style would be its creation by a Deathlord.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, personally, would hope that Laughing Wounds Style found enough natural synergy with Abyssal native Charms and resonance with Abyssal concepts that Abyssals found it to be a more tempting option than average, without resorting to the kludge of &quot;uh, Abyssals are just better at it, +1 and stuff.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:23:18-07:00","id":862728,"title":"","content":"A problem with the idea that a major component for the Dragon Blooded is their numbers is always going to be the fact that you only ever play one Dragon Blood, in gaming groups that are probably no larger than those of a Solar circle, in a system and setting in which running more than a few of these people as antagonists in a single scene is going to be a bit unlikely and difficult if you even try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:27:49-07:00","id":862732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862728#post862728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem with the idea that a major component for the Dragon Blooded is their numbers is always going to be the fact that you only ever play one Dragon Blood, in gaming groups that are probably no larger than those of a Solar circle, in a system and setting in which running more than a few of these people as antagonists in a single scene is going to be a bit unlikely and difficult if you even try.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Long story short: unless the dragon blooded book goes full ars magica, population balance only helps the setting but not the table?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T13:31:05-07:00","id":862734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862728#post862728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem with the idea that a major component for the Dragon Blooded is their numbers is always going to be the fact that you only ever play one Dragon Blood, in gaming groups that are probably no larger than those of a Solar circle, in a system and setting in which running more than a few of these people as antagonists in a single scene is going to be a bit unlikely and difficult if you even try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that I don't expect to ever run a fully statted Brotherhood against a fully statted Circle, PvP tournament style, I don't see the problem. Having access to the relevant rules will just help me make better and more varied QCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:01:38-07:00","id":862749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862721#post862721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;uh, Abyssals are just better at it, +1 and stuff.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If they do it shittily then it will indeed be shit, yes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:39:32-07:00","id":862761,"title":"","content":"I think the root problem is more of an acceptance that multi-splat games are the norm, and not a weird outlier that you need to have proper planning and exceptions for. Once you internalize that multi-splat games are the norm, you begin tacitly thinking the game ought to consider them in every written word and that the game's base balance and themes revolve around them. They don't. So, while you may not like the solution, accepting that multi-splat games are typically your table's problem and not the line's problem is a better approach and leads to resolved cases and (continues) to make the people going on about this at great length for no reason look like howler monkeys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:42:45-07:00","id":862765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862761#post862761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the root problem is more of an acceptance that multi-splat games are the norm, and not a weird outlier that you need to have proper planning and exceptions for. Once you internalize that multi-splat games are the norm, you begin tacitly thinking the game ought to consider them in every written word and that the game's base balance and themes revolve around them. They don't. So, while you may not like the solution, accepting that multi-splat games are typically your table's problem and not the line's problem is a better approach and leads to resolved cases and (continues) to make the people going on about this at great length for no reason look like howler monkeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that using a couple of specific Charm Trees to address the issue of &quot;multi-splat&quot; balance effectively reduces the options available for such games to those specific Charm Trees. That's kind of terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:43:55-07:00","id":862767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862765#post862765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that using a couple of specific Charm Trees to address the issue of &quot;multi-splat&quot; balance effectively reduces the options available for such games to those specific Charm Trees. That's kind of terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can't handle balancing multi-splat games at your table you shouldn't be playing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:47:12-07:00","id":862771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862767#post862767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can't handle balancing multi-splat games at your table you shouldn't be playing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The process is made harder if the game deliberately throws off the internal balance of certain types of Exalted by introducing a few Charm Trees designed to operate on a different scale than the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:49:41-07:00","id":862773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862761#post862761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the root problem is more of an acceptance that multi-splat games are the norm, and not a weird outlier that you need to have proper planning and exceptions for. Once you internalize that multi-splat games are the norm, you begin tacitly thinking the game ought to consider them in every written word and that the game's base balance and themes revolve around them. They don't. So, while you may not like the solution, accepting that multi-splat games are typically your table's problem and not the line's problem is a better approach and leads to resolved cases and (continues) to make the people going on about this at great length for no reason look like howler monkeys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multi-splat games ARE the norm, though, as far as my experience goes. Campaigns are, by and large, either Solar only or multi splat. I don't think I've ever seen a game of all Lunars or all Sidereals, and I have seen all of one all-Dragonblooded one. So by the time you're making more splats, multi splat IS, in fact, a concern. Either make the other splats actually bring something to the table in a multi-splat game or take a page from a <i>lot </i>of other games and don't bloody make them playable splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:51:55-07:00","id":862774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862771#post862771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The process is made harder if the game deliberately throws off the internal balance of certain types of Exalted by introducing a few Charm Trees designed to operate on a different scale than the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't play multi-splat games. They inherently ask more of you as ST's and players. This is a given, and it's obvious. The splats are not designed to be equal. They never were. EX3 is more than ever an edition of judgement calls as a ruleset, and not worrying about how people can wreck it terribly. It relies on the hand of the ST to work a lot of that stuff out, and if you haven't the steady hand of a practiced ST or a group who can adjust, don't do it or learn how. Naked systemic analysis is pointless and dumb in a game who's principles don't even value those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:53:30-07:00","id":862777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862773#post862773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Multi-splat games ARE the norm, though, as far as my experience goes. Campaigns are, by and large, either Solar only or multi splat. I don't think I've ever seen a game of all Lunars or all Sidereals, and I have seen all of one all-Dragonblooded one. So by the time you're making more splats, multi splat IS, in fact, a concern. Either make the other splats actually bring something to the table in a multi-splat game or take a page from a <i>lot </i>of other games and don't bloody make them playable splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware of according to polls taken by the developers on this specific issue, this is wrong.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T14:57:11-07:00","id":862779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862774#post862774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then don't play multi-splat games. They inherently ask more of you as ST's and players. This is a given, and it's obvious. The splats are not designed to be equal. They never were. EX3 is more than ever an edition of judgement calls as a ruleset, and not worrying about how people can wreck it terribly. It relies on the hand of the ST to work a lot of that stuff out, and if you haven't the steady hand of a practiced ST or a group who can adjust, don't do it or learn how. Naked systemic analysis is pointless and dumb in a game who's principles don't even value those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>What the... what are you talking about? You're the only one who even started talking about &quot;multi-splat games,&quot; and nothing anybody said has anything to do with being willing or able to do the work required to deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:01:39-07:00","id":862783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862779#post862779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the... what are you talking about? You're the only one who even started talking about &quot;multi-splat games,&quot; and nothing anybody said has anything to do with being willing or able to do the work required to deal with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty self evident. If multi-splat games didn't happen, would people really be complaining about power disparity and access? Would people be carrying flags for their splats if the environment in which they were played didn't, for them, involve potential marginalization via mechanics because you are mixing them together? The entire crux of this issue is a dick waving contest about splat power and marginalization. That's all it ever was. I offer up the position that complaining about this requires a tacit acceptance that multi-splat games are the norm and mechanics should be considerate of that fact at all times. The IMA issue is a microcosm of the larger &quot;issue&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:03:29-07:00","id":862784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862777#post862777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I'm aware of according to polls taken by the developers on this specific issue, this is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very unscientifically, as far as I can tell, games break down roughly along these lines:<br /> <br /> ~50% of Exalted games are Solar-only.<br /> <br /> ~40-43% of Exalted games are mixed-splat, almost universally including at least one Solar, and most often including at least half the group as Solars.<br /> <br /> ~7-10% of Exalted games are pure non-Solar, most often all-DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:08:31-07:00","id":862789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862783#post862783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty self evident. If multi-splat games didn't happen, would people really be complaining about power disparity and access? Would people be carrying flags for their splats if the environment in which they were played didn't, for them, involve potential marginalization via mechanics because you are mixing them together? The entire crux of this issue is a dick waving contest about splat power and marginalization. That's all it ever was. I offer up the position that complaining about this requires a tacit acceptance that multi-splat games are the norm and mechanics should be considerate of that fact at all times. The IMA issue is a microcosm of the larger &quot;issue&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>... except very few of the arguments being made - specifically, none of mine - were in any way about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:08:53-07:00","id":862791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862784#post862784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~40-43% of Exalted games are mixed-splat, almost universally including at least one Solar, and most often including at least half the group as Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me. I'm sure I wouldn't be the only one that would appreciate some storytelling and mechanical suggestions of how to manage multi-splat parties in future books. Possible handicaps methods, suggestions on how to manage the kind of player problems that might arise, that sort of thing. Does that sound like the kind of thing that you might include?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:14:02-07:00","id":862793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862789#post862789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... except very few of the arguments being made - specifically, none of mine - were in any way about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did address all of those with this sentence: &quot;Naked systemic analysis is pointless and dumb in a game who's principles don't even value those things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hence my shift to the more organic problem of actually playing and actual at-the-table problems. Not imaginary made up ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:16:58-07:00","id":862794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862793#post862793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did address all of those with this sentence: &quot;Naked systemic analysis is pointless and dumb in a game who's principles don't even value those things.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hence my shift to the more organic problem of actually playing and actual at-the-table problems. Not imaginary made up ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;No, YOUR concern isn't relevant!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:19:18-07:00","id":862796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862794#post862794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No, YOUR concern isn't relevant!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you for finally acquiescing to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:23:49-07:00","id":862798,"title":"","content":"In my own experience I tend to restrict players to a specific splat. My players prefer Lunars and Solars, I tend to use Abyssals and Dragon Blooded as the villains. If I ran a Dragon Blooded campaign I imagine that with a bit of work the players could triumph against a Solar antagonist because that is what heroes do win. I imagine that such a campaign would take a toll on the players and would involve dealing first with the mortal agents of the Solar, then any Exalted companions or servants before a climatic fight with the Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:24:35-07:00","id":862799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862791#post862791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me. I'm sure I wouldn't be the only one that would appreciate some storytelling and mechanical suggestions of how to manage multi-splat parties in future books. Possible handicaps methods, suggestions on how to manage the kind of player problems that might arise, that sort of thing. Does that sound like the kind of thing that you might include?</div> </div> </div> </div>Run them straight out of the books. They're written for crossover play; it is the default assumption for everyone other than DBs. I will never, ever suggest handicapping, I think it is a bad practice that misunderstands mixed groups in Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:25:05-07:00","id":862800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862796#post862796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, thank you for finally acquiescing to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind the smartass laconic comeback if it actually made sense, but as far as I can see you are either thanking him for acquiescing that <i>your </i>concern isn't relevant or thanking him for quoting you in summary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862799#post862799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Run them straight out of the books. They're written for crossover play; it is the default assumption for everyone other than DBs. I will never, ever suggest handicapping, I think it is a bad practice that misunderstands mixed groups in Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on that a bit? To take an extreme, I would never begrudge a player who wanted to run a mortal in a game with Exalts a few extra bonus points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 04-09-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:27:55-07:00","id":862801,"title":"","content":"What Holden said does seem to about align with the experience I mentioned. Games are almost universally either pure Solar, or mixed splat. Single splat games of other types are vanishingly rare. Usually at least one Solar in the mix somewhere (sometimes another Solaroid takes the position, but most often it's a Solar). Mixed splat games do happen often enough to be more of a norm than not the instant we get out of Solars. <br /> <br /> So with this being as it is, other splats should either bring different, fun, and useful contributions to a mixed splat party, or one should really think on whether we should just make Solars the only playable splat. Because people clearly don't share your view that mixed-splat play is &quot;minor&quot; and &quot;not relevant to actual at a table play&quot;, ParanoiaCombo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:28:19-07:00","id":862802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862800#post862800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't mind the smartass laconic comeback if it actually made sense, but as far as I can see you are either thanking him for acquiescing that <i>your </i>concern isn't relevant or thanking him for quoting you in summary.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was attempting to characterize my post as me saying that to him.<br /> Which I was.<br /> <br /> So I thanked him for finally getting it. A little politeness goes a long way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:30:25-07:00","id":862803,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm not getting something, but all those threads feel like exercises in overthinking it. Solars aren't &quot;better than you&quot;. They've got an epic, heroic niche they fill, just like the other splats. Maybe it's because I've never played the old editions, so I don't have years of Solars dick-slapping everything into submission to look back on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:31:46-07:00","id":862804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862802#post862802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I thanked him for finally getting it. A little politeness goes a long way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because when you're being rude and dismissive, and the other person points out that you're being rude and dismissive, a little politeness appears that much greater in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:32:49-07:00","id":862806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862801#post862801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Holden said does seem to about align with the experience I mentioned. Games are almost universally either pure Solar, or mixed splat. Single splat games of other types are vanishingly rare. Usually at least one Solar in the mix somewhere (sometimes another Solaroid takes the position, but most often it's a Solar). Mixed splat games do happen often enough to be more of a norm than not the instant we get out of Solars.<br /> <br /> So with this being as it is, other splats should either bring different, fun, and useful contributions to a mixed splat party, or one should really think on whether we should just make Solars the only playable splat. Because people clearly don't share your view that mixed-splat play is &quot;minor&quot; and &quot;not relevant to actual at a table play&quot;, ParanoiaCombo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is people are making disparity into &quot;if disparity exists in a way I don't like, we might as well just play all Solars&quot;. That is stupid and wrong. It takes chops to do it right. I don't know what else to tell you other than &quot;gain the necessary chops, because if you dislike how the game is written with regards to certain things you are gonna have a bad time.&quot; Real power differences and disparities are part of the game. They sometimes lead to hurt feelings or bad results which are mitigated at the table- not in the books. The books make things crystal clear that splats are different and not intended for as much parity as many people seem to want or think &quot;should&quot; be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:33:33-07:00","id":862808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862804#post862804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because when you're being rude and dismissive, and the other person points out that you're being rude and dismissive, a little politeness appears that much greater in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>See now we are thinking on the same level. Thank you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:38:06-07:00","id":862810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862803#post862803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm not getting something, but all those threads feel like exercises in overthinking it. Solars aren't &quot;better than you&quot;. They've got an epic, heroic niche they fill, just like the other splats. Maybe it's because I've never played the old editions, so I don't have years of Solars dick-slapping everything into submission to look back on?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's about the size of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:41:09-07:00","id":862811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862800#post862800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you elaborate on that a bit? To take an extreme, I would never begrudge a player who wanted to run a mortal in a game with Exalts a few extra bonus points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, to turn it back around-- why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:42:33-07:00","id":862812,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth...I couldn't care less about DB vs Solar balance, but I think using the same mechanics for a Martial Art available to both is likely to mess up the internal balance of one, the other, or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:46:05-07:00","id":862814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862812#post862812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth...I couldn't care less about DB vs Solar balance, but I think using the same mechanics for a Martial Art available to both is likely to mess up the internal balance of one, the other, or both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, the answer Holden gave actually addressed that pretty well, albeit by throwing out what I felt was the most elegant aspect of the Martial Arts system. It can be as balanced for Dragon-Blooded as it ever was, and it's just not intended to be an attractive choice for anyone with access to the Mastery Keyword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:50:19-07:00","id":862816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862810#post862810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's about the size of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to see I've got a good grasp of the issue at hand, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:55:12-07:00","id":862819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862814#post862814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, the answer Holden gave actually addressed that pretty well, albeit by throwing out what I felt was the most elegant aspect of the Martial Arts system. It can be as balanced for Dragon-Blooded as it ever was, and it's just not intended to be an attractive choice for anyone with access to the Mastery Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *shrug*<br /> <br /> I mean, a Solar with Fire Dragon Style is still going to kick the living shit out of just about anything he fights. Any MA style is very frightening when backed by Solar mote pools, Athletics Charms, Awareness Charms, Resistance Charms, etc. You can mow down blood apes aplenty with it. You certainly won't be feeling <i>deprived</i>. It's just not the strongest option you could have picked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:56:17-07:00","id":862820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862816#post862816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad to see I've got a good grasp of the issue at hand, then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> P much. The last edition had a lot of very confrontational design and balance issues that produced lingering resentment. It's just not really going to be an issue worth worrying about from now on tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:04:39-07:00","id":862825,"title":"","content":"That's exactly the direction I was hoping you <i>wouldn't</i> take.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a good thing if Solar Fire Dragon is noticeably worse than Solar Steel Devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:07:09-07:00","id":862827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862819#post862819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug*<br /> <br /> I mean, a Solar with Fire Dragon Style is still going to kick the living shit out of just about anything he fights. Any MA style is very frightening when backed by Solar mote pools, Athletics Charms, Awareness Charms, Resistance Charms, etc. You can mow down blood apes aplenty with it. You certainly won't be feeling <i>deprived</i>. It's just not the strongest option you could have picked.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's cool, but now I have to draw a distinction I never thought I had to - between &quot;powerful and dreaded martial arts secrets,&quot; and &quot;powerful, dreaded, and <i>coveted</i> martial arts secrets.&quot; It's great that my Solars will have to worry about Immaculates hunting them down, because they're a challenge, but if they're offered a chance to learn their enemies' most potent kung fu to use against them, instead of eagerly leaping at the opportunity, it's now the more sensible option to look at the limited available XP and say &quot;y'know, I heard there's a Tiger sifu not far from here...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","user":"Ren9077","date":".  Grammar 04-09-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:21:41-07:00","id":862830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862827#post862827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's cool, but now I have to draw a distinction I never thought I had to - between &quot;powerful and dreaded martial arts secrets,&quot; and &quot;powerful, dreaded, and <i>coveted</i> martial arts secrets.&quot; It's great that my Solars will have to worry about Immaculates hunting them down, because they're a challenge, but if they're offered a chance to learn their enemies' most potent kung fu to use against them, instead of eagerly leaping at the opportunity, it's now the more sensible option to look at the limited available XP and say &quot;y'know, I heard there's a Tiger sifu not far from here...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are unfortunately trade-offs for everything, but what I'm thinking of is that the great strength of Martial Arts styles does not lie solely within a single style tree, but how you mix and match them with other styles. A Snake stylist is going to be much harder to kill with some Crane backing him up, and Ebon Shadow shinobi is most definitely not going to regret picking up Tiger style.<br /> <br /> So, perhaps Fire Dragon style (for example) synergizes really, really well with, say, Snake style that makes the loss of Mastery effects worth it.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not. Maybe Solar characters just have to deal with not being the best at something that wasn't made for them. I wouldn't mind.<br /> <br /> Edit: Speaking of which, are there going to be other styles mentioned in the DB book, the ones that secular DBs learn? Like Even Blade and Five Dragon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 04-09-2016, 07:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:28:59-07:00","id":862832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862830#post862830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Solar characters just have to deal with not being the best at something that wasn't made for them. I wouldn't mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most thrown-around line in the entire discussion, and it's just weird. No one's saying &quot;OMG SOLARS CAN'T NOT BE THE BEST THAT'S WRONG!&quot; What I - and possibly Sanctaphrax also - am saying is that, in character, the Immaculates have some awesome and exclusive martial arts secrets that anyone in their right mind would covet, but out of character, anyone with access to the Mastery keyword would be better served spending that XP on something else, and that's kind of weird and disjointed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:29:11-07:00","id":862833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862827#post862827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's cool, but now I have to draw a distinction I never thought I had to - between &quot;powerful and dreaded martial arts secrets,&quot; and &quot;powerful, dreaded, and <i>coveted</i> martial arts secrets.&quot; It's great that my Solars will have to worry about Immaculates hunting them down, because they're a challenge, but if they're offered a chance to learn their enemies' most potent kung fu to use against them, instead of eagerly leaping at the opportunity, it's now the more sensible option to look at the limited available XP and say &quot;y'know, I heard there's a Tiger sifu not far from here...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, you could not look at the game like it's entirely about resource management tradeoffs. There are a lot of games which reward that kind of thinking, but RPGs rarely are one of them unless they are specifically designed to be that kind of game. This isn't a game flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:31:04-07:00","id":862834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862825#post862825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly the direction I was hoping you <i>wouldn't</i> take.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a good thing if Solar Fire Dragon is noticeably worse than Solar Steel Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It won't particularly matter in actual play, and as such, is really not worth worrying about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:32:21-07:00","id":862835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862827#post862827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's cool, but now I have to draw a distinction I never thought I had to - between &quot;powerful and dreaded martial arts secrets,&quot; and &quot;powerful, dreaded, and <i>coveted</i> martial arts secrets.&quot; It's great that my Solars will have to worry about Immaculates hunting them down, because they're a challenge, but if they're offered a chance to learn their enemies' most potent kung fu to use against them, instead of eagerly leaping at the opportunity, it's now the more sensible option to look at the limited available XP and say &quot;y'know, I heard there's a Tiger sifu not far from here...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, dude, I'm going to say something to you that may well blow your mind. Seriously, sit down, otherwise you may pass out and hit your head.<br /> <br /> You ready? You sure?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not everyone gives a flying fire truck about Mechanical Optimization</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Crazy, I know! But some people prioritize interesting character concepts over &quot;What gives me the most pluses?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:34:13-07:00","id":862836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862833#post862833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, you know, you could not look at the game like it's entirely about resource management tradeoffs. There are a lot of games which reward that kind of thinking, but RPGs rarely are one of them unless they are specifically designed to be that kind of game. This isn't a game flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead of posting to tell me that the way I think about the game is fundamentally flawed, maybe your time could be better spent <i>not</i> doing that. Like, type what you just typed, only before you do, turn your chair 90 degrees so that your fingers aren't touching the keyboard. That would be so much nicer.<br /> <br /> For a game that's not about resource management tradeoffs, Essence and Willpower totals start looking pretty freaking important after a few rounds, and you'd be surprised at how many Storytellers are sticklers about not letting you use Charms that aren't actually on your sheet because you didn't have enough XP to buy them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:36:19-07:00","id":862837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862835#post862835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, dude, I'm going to say something to you that may well blow your mind. Seriously, sit down, otherwise you may pass out and hit your head.<br /> <br /> You ready? You sure?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Not everyone gives a flying fire truck about Mechanical Optimization</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Crazy, I know! But some people prioritize interesting character concepts over &quot;What gives me the most pluses?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you one of those people who plays <i>Exalted</i> with Fate, then? Because this is an awfully crunchy system to not care about where the numbers are. A few of the combats I've run have come down to a difference of one or two motes, or one success. Charm selection <i>matters.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:39:51-07:00","id":862840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862836#post862836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of posting to tell me that the way I think about the game is fundamentally flawed, maybe your time could be better spent <i>not</i> doing that. Like, type what you just typed, only before you do, turn your chair 90 degrees so that your fingers aren't touching the keyboard. That would be so much nicer.<br /> <br /> For a game that's not about resource management tradeoffs, Essence and Willpower totals start looking pretty freaking important after a few rounds, and you'd be surprised at how many Storytellers are sticklers about not letting you use Charms that aren't actually on your sheet because you didn't have enough XP to buy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are free to continue being miserable about something you can't change, while I remain happy and actually solve the problems that come up at the table. If that's how you want it to be, then fine. If you don't want to accept that an approach to a game can cause you problems and offload them onto the text, that's fine too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:40:15-07:00","id":862841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862832#post862832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the most thrown-around line in the entire discussion, and it's just weird. No one's saying &quot;OMG SOLARS CAN'T NOT BE THE BEST THAT'S WRONG!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen this viewpoint espoused so often that I have a knee-jerk reaction against it, my apologies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862832#post862832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I - and possibly Sanctaphrax also - am saying is that, in character, the Immaculates have some awesome and exclusive martial arts secrets that anyone in their right mind would covet, but out of character, anyone with access to the Mastery keyword would be better served spending that XP on something else, and that's kind of weird and disjointed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a compromise, yes. But I'm willing to make that compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:41:07-07:00","id":862842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862837#post862837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charm selection <i>matters.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. And Martial Arts styles, in particular -- all of them -- are about trade-offs and picking a particular specialized fighting style to excel at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:41:53-07:00","id":862843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862819#post862819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> *shrug*<br /> <br /> I mean, a Solar with Fire Dragon Style is still going to kick the living shit out of just about anything he fights. Any MA style is very frightening when backed by Solar mote pools, Athletics Charms, Awareness Charms, Resistance Charms, etc. You can mow down blood apes aplenty with it. You certainly won't be feeling <i>deprived</i>. It's just not the strongest option you could have picked.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've made me a happy forumite. You and your beautiful books. <br /> <br /> This is very nice to hear, personally. Sounds like itll be good to homebrew for people who want that, and a great default for the baseline. Im excited to see its implementation when it finally releases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:43:02-07:00","id":862845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862840#post862840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are free to continue being miserable about something you can't change, while I remain happy and actually solve the problems that come up at the table. If that's how you want it to be, then fine. If you don't want to accept that an approach to a game can cause you problems and offload them onto the text, that's fine too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for posting to tell me how miserable I am and how much better and happier you are than me.<br /> <br /> Remember when you were banned for this sort of aggressive behavior? Like, last week? Good times, good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:47:45-07:00","id":862847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's a good thing if Solar Fire Dragon is noticeably worse than Solar Steel Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Not the best option&quot; is not equivalent to &quot;noticeably worse than&quot;. Depending on what your priorities are, any Martial Art whatsoever might not be the best option compared to Solar combat Charms or Evocations. Define what Fire Dragon actually does; define what Steel Devil actually does; define what Dreaming Pearl Courtesan actually does; choose the one that suits your desired goals and playstyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:48:20-07:00","id":862848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862837#post862837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you one of those people who plays <i>Exalted</i> with Fate, then? Because this is an awfully crunchy system to not care about where the numbers are. A few of the combats I've run have come down to a difference of one or two motes, or one success. Charm selection <i>matters.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I played flat second edition as my first introduction, I play a 2.5 game online. In that five year span from my first game to now, It's the first time i've ever needed to use a perfect defense. Know why i used a perfect defense? To dodge the explosive i slapped onto my fist as i drove it into a monster.<br /> <br /> I had a dragon blood kill a second circle demon using a throw attack. I had 0 dots of throw, and dex 4. Amazing what a 3 die stunt, cooperation, and just straight up brass balls can do for you (virtue channel) when you are also smart about it. She was essence 2, a water aspect with no combat charms other than Safety Among Enemies. (Not even an offensive excellency)<br /> <br /> This was of course after using a haddock as a skateboard upon a dock to catch up to someone.<br /> <br /> Long story short,<br /> <br /> Sure i could have made an optimized combat DB. But that wasn't my concept, and it didn't hurt me in the slightest that i wasn't even 5s in my chosen field.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:48:36-07:00","id":862849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862845#post862845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much for posting to tell me how miserable I am and how much better and happier you are than me.<br /> <br /> Remember when you were banned for this sort of aggressive behavior? Like, last week? Good times, good times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked this post.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:49:13-07:00","id":862850,"title":"","content":"A Solar picking up an IMA still kicks flaming booty. A Dragon-Blooded picking native charms is still a force to be reckoned with.<br /> <br /> The important thing is that a player always feels powerful and/or useful, not that every possible action is mechanically optimal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:53:35-07:00","id":862854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862842#post862842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm. And Martial Arts styles, in particular -- all of them -- are about trade-offs and picking a particular specialized fighting style to excel at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them, however, are not in any way marked &quot;Not For You&quot; and deliberately less powerful than the others.<br /> <br /> You assure me that the difference is inconsequential, and that's cool... but the core book has 11 styles. I know they're not all perfectly balanced against each other, but they all seem to be in roughly the same ballpark, and I don't think you set out to make some stronger or weaker than the others. That's eleven boxes of approximately equal awesomeness I can choose from. Now, in talking about five OTHER boxes of awesomeness - guaranteed to contain at least 90-95% as much awesome! - well, that's substantial awesomeness, but why choose the box that is intentionally not as awesome as the alternatives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:55:35-07:00","id":862856,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that tabletop games in the past have sometimes had mechanical failure states where the game becomes pretty unfun for someone at the table. Playing eg. 3e D&amp;D as a fighter in a game where a wizard goes all out is often not very fun (because encounters will come down to &quot;what spell does the wizard use to resolve this&quot; -- all the important tactical options end up being made by the casters, leaving non-casters feeling like they're not really playing.) Ex2 had a lot of similar-ish failure states it could fall into -- though to be fair, even at its worst Exalted has never, in my experience, been as bad as D&amp;D has been at its worst in terms of the &quot;why does your character even bother to show up for fights?&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> 3e D&amp;D also has a unique problem where most of your choices are irrevocable and where it's entirely possible for a bad decision to leave your character basically mechanically non-functional. (eg. trying to build a fighter-mage by taking equal numbers of levels of fighter and mage levels, which <i>looks</i> like a logical option at first glance, will lead to a character that is barely able to contribute mechanically at all.) Past experiences like these leave a lot of tabletop gamers paranoid that the game's mechanics are going to fall apart on them if they make the wrong choices.<br /> <br /> (I think growing up playing a certain kind of videogame leads to this, too, because unlike a tabletop game a badly-designed videogame doesn't have any way of recognizing that you've built a low-power character, and will proceed to crush you mercilessly.)<br /> <br /> But Ex3, at least so far, seems a lot more robust. The basic nature of the combat system means that having an additional combatant on your side with any sort of meaningful combat stats at all is always valuable and always puts more pressure on the enemy, while ensuring that nobody can just be casually taken out of a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:56:30-07:00","id":862858,"title":"","content":"&quot;The most incredible thing about arguing on the Internet is that you don't need to stop anywhere.&quot;<br /> -Actually a quote about changing things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T16:59:07-07:00","id":862859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862837#post862837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you one of those people who plays <i>Exalted</i> with Fate, then? Because this is an awfully crunchy system to not care about where the numbers are. A few of the combats I've run have come down to a difference of one or two motes, or one success. Charm selection <i>matters.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I run an Exalted game every week using Ex3's rules. I've been doing it since February of last year, once I got my hands on the leak. I've seen Martial Artists, Melee, Thrown, Archers, and Brawlers played on my games.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that NONE of them are optimized.<br /> <br /> I'm certain that all of them are having fun.<br /> <br /> Everyone does SOMETHING, I go out of my way to include everyone in SOME capacity, even if it's just for a small character-driven segment with them chatting with NPCs.<br /> <br /> We use 99.9% RAW. We're not having any major troubles.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah. I think that &quot;I don't care about mechanical optimization, I just want to play a character that's fun&quot; is a valid mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:07:59-07:00","id":862866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862859#post862859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run an Exalted game every week using Ex3's rules. I've been doing it since February of last year, once I got my hands on the leak. I've seen Martial Artists, Melee, Thrown, Archers, and Brawlers played on my games.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure that NONE of them are optimized.<br /> <br /> I'm certain that all of them are having fun.<br /> <br /> Everyone does SOMETHING, I go out of my way to include everyone in SOME capacity, even if it's just for a small character-driven segment with them chatting with NPCs.<br /> <br /> We use 99.9% RAW. We're not having any major troubles.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah. I think that &quot;I don't care about mechanical optimization, I just want to play a character that's fun&quot; is a valid mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the combat gets challenging, which is fun. When combat is challenging and fun, the players are poring over their sheets, trying to figure out how to best use the resources they have to make a difference. Moments like these are the entire point of playing a game with the kind of mechanical heft <i>Exalted</i> has. Many players actually like to plan ahead for those moments, and build their characters in a way that, while not 100% spreadsheet-optimized, shows some intelligence and foresight. This is inevitable in - encouraged by, even - a game that has mechanical heft. And then people like you and ParanoiaCombo come along and tell me that I'm <i>doing it wrong.</i><br /> <br /> This is why I hate Internet roleplaying communities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:13:55-07:00","id":862870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862866#post862866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes the combat gets challenging, which is fun. When combat is challenging and fun, the players are poring over their sheets, trying to figure out how to best use the resources they have to make a difference. Moments like these are the entire point of playing a game with the kind of mechanical heft <i>Exalted</i> has. Many players actually like to plan ahead for those moments, and build their characters in a way that, while not 100% spreadsheet-optimized, shows some intelligence and foresight. This is inevitable in - encouraged by, even - a game that has mechanical heft. And then people like you and ParanoiaCombo come along and tell me that I'm <i>doing it wrong.</i><br /> <br /> This is why I hate Internet roleplaying communities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know what game is really good at providing this kind of experience? DnD 4E. You know why it's good at providing this kind of experience? Because it was intentionally designed to have an on-the-rails progression and expected levels of challenge for which to calibrate all those numbers to. Do you really think Exalted has this, or has any ability to reproduce this? It does not. There is no CR or equivalent. There is no intention to have that. All the balancing and encounter design is done by the ST, which means it can flux, and vary wildly in whether your mechanical choices actually matter from scene to scene. You are imposing a standard onto a game that has no use for such a standard. Different games are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:16:17-07:00","id":862872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862870#post862870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what game is really good at providing this kind of experience? DnD 4E. You know why it's good at providing this kind of experience? Because it was intentionally designed to have an on-the-rails progression and expected levels of challenge for which to calibrate all those numbers to. Do you really think Exalted has this, or has any ability to reproduce this? It does not. There is no CR or equivalent. There is no intention to have that. All the balancing and encounter design is done by the ST, which means it can flux, and vary wildly in whether your mechanical choices actually matter from scene to scene. You are imposing a standard onto a game that has no use for such a standard. Different games are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for informing me that combat in <i>Exalted Third Edition</i>, with all the work that it entails, is not meant to be challenging or fun. I bet that's exactly what John and Holden were going for - dry, tedious accounting for its own sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:17:19-07:00","id":862873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862866#post862866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I hate Internet roleplaying communities.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's fun for you, it's fun for you. I've NEVER told you not to have fun.<br /> <br /> YOU are the one who said &quot;Why should I buy an IMA for my Solar when it's more optimal to buy say, Steel Devil?&quot;, you're the one who assumed that nobody would make a Solar who uses an IMA because it's suboptimal.<br /> <br /> And when people say &quot;Er, I'd do it. I don't care about optimization, I just want to make an interesting character&quot;, you start playing the victim.<br /> <br /> And I don't recall a single person saying that you're doing this wrong. YOU seem to be the one complaining about how the Immaculate Styles won't give an extra bonus to Solars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:17:24-07:00","id":862874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862866#post862866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I hate Internet roleplaying communities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony, it burns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:18:25-07:00","id":862876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862872#post862872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for informing me that combat in <i>Exalted Third Edition</i>, with all the work that it entails, is not meant to be challenging or fun. I bet that's exactly what John and Holden were going for - dry, tedious accounting for its own sake.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you have to read it to escape the obvious central point, more power to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:20:11-07:00","id":862880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861879-regarding-the-aggiecon-thread-and-solars?p=862873#post862873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's fun for you, it's fun for you. I've NEVER told you not to have fun.<br /> <br /> YOU are the one who said &quot;Why should I buy an IMA for my Solar when it's more optimal to buy say, Steel Devil?&quot;, you're the one who assumed that nobody would make a Solar who uses an IMA because it's suboptimal.<br /> <br /> And when people say &quot;Er, I'd do it. I don't care about optimization, I just want to make an interesting character&quot;, you start playing the victim.<br /> <br /> And I don't recall a single person saying that you're doing this wrong. YOU seem to be the one complaining about how the Immaculate Styles won't give an extra bonus to Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaand, we're back to misrepresenting my argument. Yup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","cust